        ages: 24...55,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A three-year-old found a loaded pistol in a backpack hanging in {D}'s hallway on {DATE} and fired it, wounding {V}, a six-year-old cousin, in the thigh. {V} was released after two nights in the hospital. {DL} says the backpack was zipped and out of reach until a visiting relative moved it.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Pistol", "A loaded pistol with a round chambered, found beside the open backpack."), E(.document, 2, "Purchase Receipt", "{DL} bought the pistol two months before and also bought a lockbox, which was never opened."), E(.statement, 1, "Deputy", "No lock was on the pistol or the backpack.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Moved Bag", "{DL} says a visiting relative took the backpack down and set it on a bench.")],
        role: "Sheriff's deputy",
        exam: [.direct("Where was the pistol when you arrived?", "\"Next to an open backpack on the hall bench. The backpack had hung in the hallway, and the pistol was lying beside it.\""), .direct("Was it loaded?", "\"A round in the chamber. The pistol was ready to fire, and a single round had already been discharged.\""), .direct("Who was hurt?", "\"{V}, a six-year-old cousin, wounded in the thigh. A three-year-old had found the pistol and fired it.\""), .direct("How was {V} treated?", "\"At the hospital for two nights, then released. The wound was serious, but doctors expected a full recovery.\""), .direct("What did you learn about the purchase?", "\"{D} bought the pistol two months earlier and also bought a lockbox at the same time, according to the receipt.\""), .direct("Where was the lockbox?", "\"Unopened, in the closet. It was still in its packaging, and the key and instructions were inside.\""), .cross("Was the pocket zipped?", "\"I cannot say when it was opened. I found it open, and I do not know what state it was in earlier.\""), .cross("Was there a lock on the pistol or the backpack?", "\"No. Neither had a lock, and I wrote that in my report.\""), .cross("Did {D} cooperate?", "\"Yes. {D.He} called 911 right away, handed over the pistol, and stayed with {V} until help arrived.\""), .cross("Did you speak with the visiting relative?", "\"Yes. The relative said the backpack was moved to make room, and the relative did not know about the pistol.\""), .cross("Did the defendant say where the backpack had been kept?", "\"Yes. {D.He} said it hung up high, zipped, until the visitor moved it.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Visiting relative",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Why were you at {D}'s home?", "\"I was visiting for a few days, and I was staying in a spare room near the hallway.\""), .direct("Did you move the backpack?", "\"Yes, to make room. There was a coat and a bag pile, and I needed space on the hook and the bench.\""), .direct("Where was it before you moved it?", "\"On a hook, up high, and zipped shut. I lifted it down and set it on the bench.\""), .direct("Did you know a pistol was in it?", "\"No. I had no idea. If I had known, I would never have set it down where a child could reach.\""), .direct("Where were the children?", "\"Playing in the living room. The three-year-old wandered into the hall while we were in the kitchen.\""), .direct("How did you react when you heard the shot?", "\"I ran into the hall and saw {V} on the floor. I grabbed a towel and pressed it on the wound.\""), .cross("Did you check the backpack when you moved it?", "\"No. It was zipped, and I did not look inside.\""), .cross("Did the defendant tell you what was in the pack?", "\"No. {D} never mentioned it, and I never would have touched it if I knew.\""), .cross("Did you tell the defendant you moved it?", "\"I told {DF} afterward. I said I had put it on the bench, and {DF} was shocked.\""), .cross("Was the pack heavy?", "\"A little heavier than I expected. I thought it had books in it.\""), .cross("Are you blaming yourself?", "\"Yes, a little. I should have asked before moving someone else's bag.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} left a loaded pistol where children could reach it.", "A zipped bag moved by someone else."),
        allocution: "\"I should have used that lockbox. I'm so sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had been warned by the child's parent about a loaded gun in the house the month before.", "{DL} had kept the pistol in a zipped pocket on a high hook until the relative moved it."),
        defendant: [.direct("Was the pistol loaded?", "\"Yes. I kept it loaded for protection, and I should have kept it locked up instead.\""), .direct("Where did you keep it?", "\"On a high hook in the hallway, in a zipped pocket of a backpack, well out of reach of the children.\""), .direct("What about the lockbox?", "\"I had not set it up yet. I bought it with the pistol and meant to install it, and I did not.\""), .direct("What changed that day?", "\"A visiting relative moved the backpack to make room. I did not know it had been moved until I heard the shot.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I ran into the hall, grabbed {V}, called 911, and pressed on the wound until the paramedics came.\""), .direct("What do you want the family to know?", "\"I am so sorry. I should never have kept a loaded pistol in a backpack in the house, and I will never forgive myself.\""), .cross("You kept a loaded pistol with a round chambered, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I know now that was a serious mistake.\""), .cross("You bought a lockbox and never opened it, didn't you?", "\"That is right. I put it off, and I regret that more than anything.\""), .cross("There were three small children in your home, weren't there?", "\"Yes. That makes it worse. I should have known better.\""), .cross("The pistol was found beside an open backpack on a bench, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. The relative moved it there, but it was still my pistol and my home.\""), .cross("A six-year-old was shot, wasn't {V}?", "\"Yes. {V} is my cousin, and I think of it every day.\"")],
        openings: ("A three-year-old found a loaded pistol in a backpack in {D}'s hallway and fired it, wounding {V}, a six-year-old cousin, in the thigh. {D} had bought a lockbox with the pistol two months earlier and never opened it.", "The backpack hung zipped and out of reach until a visiting relative moved it to the bench. {D} made a terrible mistake, and the State must show that mistake was a crime."),
        closings: ("A loaded pistol with a round in the chamber, a lockbox still in the closet, and three small children in the house. {V} was shot because the gun was not locked up.", "A zipped pocket on a high hook, a visitor who moved the bag, and a child who found it. {D} never meant for this to happen, and nothing shows {D} was reckless."),
        timeline: [(-60, "{DL} buys the pistol and a lockbox."), (0, "Afternoon: the relative moves the backpack."), (0, "Afternoon: the shot."), (0, "Evening: {V} is in surgery.")],
        identified: "A deputy and a receipt.",
        mood: .sympathetic,
        impact: "My niece is afraid of loud noises now.")

    static let employeeIdentityTheftV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.employeeIdentityTheft",
        category: .cyber,
        headlines: ["Staffing Clerk Opened Phone Plans in Temp Workers' Names", "Account Applications Used Employee Forms From Onboarding"],
        law: "identityTheft",
        threshold: 6,
        spec: "Knowingly obtained and used the identifying information of {V} to obtain credit, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V}, a temp worker, was denied an apartment on {DATE} because of a $3,100 phone bill on an account opened in {V.his} name. The application used the Social Security number from {V}'s onboarding packet. {D}, a clerk at the staffing office, had scanned that packet the week before. {DL} says a scanner repairman had access to the files.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Account Application", "A phone plan application in {V}'s name with the number copied from the packet."), E(.digital, 3, "Scan Log", "{D}'s login scanned {V}'s packet five days before the application."), E(.document, 1, "Delivery Address", "The phones shipped to a mailbox {D} rents.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Repairman", "{DL} says a scanner technician had the files open during a repair."), E(.document, 1, "Repair Ticket", "A ticket shows a visit the same week.")],
        role: "Staffing office manager",
        exam: [.direct("Who scanned {V}'s onboarding packet?", "\"{D}, according to the scan log. {D.his} login scanned the packet five days before the phone plan application.\""), .direct("What was the packet?", "\"New hire paperwork with {V}'s Social Security number, address, and ID copies. Every worker fills one out.\""), .direct("What did the account application show?", "\"A phone plan application in {V}'s name, with the Social Security number copied exactly from the packet.\""), .direct("Where did the phones go?", "\"A mailbox rented in {D.his} name. The phones shipped there, and that is where the trail led.\""), .direct("What was the result for {V}?", "\"{V} was denied an apartment because of a $3,100 phone bill on an account {V} never opened.\""), .direct("Who else had access to the files?", "\"A scanner repairman worked on the machine that week. I will let the technician describe what was seen.\""), .cross("Did the repairman have access?", "\"For about an hour. The repairman was alone at the machine, and the files were on a shared drive.\""), .cross("Did the repairman leave a login?", "\"No. The repairman used a service login that was disabled after the repair.\""), .cross("Who else had a login to the scanning system?", "\"Three people, including {DL}. Any of them could scan a packet.\""), .cross("Is scanning packets part of {D}'s job?", "\"Yes. {D.He} scanned many packets that week, as part of normal duties.\""), .cross("Did the defendant cooperate?", "\"Yes. {D.He} answered questions and told us about the repairman.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Scanner technician",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What do you do?", "\"I am a scanner technician. I repair and service office scanners and copiers.\""), .direct("Did you work at the staffing office?", "\"Yes, for about an hour, repairing the scanner. I was in the back office with the machine.\""), .direct("Did you see staff files?", "\"I saw the screen for a bit. I needed to test the scanner, and files were on the screen.\""), .direct("Did you copy anything?", "\"Never. I did not copy, save, or write down any information, and I did not need to.\""), .direct("How do you test a scanner?", "\"I scan a few pages and check the quality. I used pages from the shared tray.\""), .direct("Did anyone watch you?", "\"Off and on. A clerk checked in, but I was alone with the machine for stretches.\""), .cross("Could you have read the files?", "\"I could have seen them on the screen. I did not read them closely.\""), .cross("Did you have access to the drive?", "\"Through the service login. It lets me test the scanner and see what it scanned.\""), .cross("Did you note down a Social Security number?", "\"No. I do not do that, and I would lose my job.\""), .cross("Did you speak to {D}?", "\"Briefly, to ask where to set up. {D} was polite and helpful.\""), .cross("How long were you alone with the machine?", "\"Maybe twenty minutes in total, in short stretches.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} used a coworker's information to open accounts.", "A repair visit exposed the files."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry. I should never have touched that packet.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} searched for how to open lines with another person's number.", "The mailbox in {DL}'s name was opened by someone using a copy of {DL}'s ID."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you open the account?", "\"No. I did not open any phone account in {V}'s name, and I did not use {V}'s number.\""), .direct("What about the mailbox?", "\"Mine, for my own packages. I rent it because my apartment does not have a secure place for deliveries.\""), .direct("Why did you scan {V}'s packet?", "\"It was my job. I scan every new packet, and I did not look at any of them beyond the scan.\""), .direct("Who else had a login?", "\"Three people. I am one of them, and the others could scan any packet too.\""), .direct("What about the repairman?", "\"The repairman was in the office for an hour with a service login, and could see the files, and I did not watch the repair.\""), .direct("What do you want {V} to know?", "\"I am sorry this happened. I did not do it, and I hope you get your credit cleared.\""), .cross("Your login scanned the packet five days before the application, didn't it?", "\"Yes. That is my job. I scanned many packets, and I did not copy a number.\""), .cross("The phones shipped to a mailbox you rent, didn't they?", "\"So they say. I did not order them, and I did not pick them up.\""), .cross("You are the only person tied to both the scan and the mailbox, aren't you?", "\"Yes. That is why I am here. It still does not mean I did it.\""), .cross("You had access to Social Security numbers every day, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I handled them every day, and I never misused one.\""), .cross("Who knew your mailbox number?", "\"Staff and a few friends. It was on a package label that came to the office once.\"")],
        openings: ("{V}, a temp worker, was denied an apartment because of a $3,100 phone bill on an account opened in {V}'s name. {D}, a clerk at the staffing office, scanned {V}'s onboarding packet five days earlier, and the phones shipped to a mailbox {D} rents.", "Three people had a login to the scanning system and a repairman had access to the files for an hour. A clerk who scanned a packet as part of the job is not a thief."),
        closings: ("{D}'s login scanned the packet, the number was copied exactly, and the phones went to {D}'s mailbox. Access and opportunity both lead to {D}.", "A shared drive, a repairman alone with the files, and a clerk who scanned hundreds of packets. The State has a log and a mailbox, but no proof {D} used a number."),
        timeline: [(-10, "{V} fills out an onboarding packet."), (-5, "{DL} scans the packet."), (0, "The application is submitted."), (14, "{V} is denied an apartment.")],
        identified: "A scan log and a mailbox rental.",
        mood: .wantsConviction)

    static let lotteryWinnerV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.lotteryWinner",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Jackpot Winner Missing for a Year; Remains Found in Pond Drain", "Business Manager Charged in Death of Man Who Won $9 Million"],
        law: "murder1",
        threshold: 10,
        spec: "With premeditation and deliberation, killed {V}, a lottery winner, by shooting {V.him} once in the head.",
        ages: 34...40,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V} won a $9 million jackpot and hired {D}, a self-described business manager, to handle {V.his} money. Within two years most of it had moved to {D}'s companies. {V} vanished. For ten months texts from {V}'s phone said {V.he} was traveling. On {DATE}, a landscaper clearing a drainage pond found a body, identified as {V}, shot once in the head. {DL} says {V} chose to disappear and that the money was a loan.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Bank Transfers", "$1.1 million from {V}'s accounts into {D}'s companies, signed by {D} under a power of attorney."), E(.digital, 3, "Travel Texts", "Texts from {V}'s phone sent from towers near {D}'s home, with {D}'s habit of dropping apostrophes."), E(.forensic, 2, "Autopsy", "One gunshot wound to the head, a .38-caliber bullet recovered."), E(.physical, 2, "Pond Search", "Divers recovered a pistol cleaning kit tied to a brick near the body.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Wanted to Disappear", "{DL} says {V} wanted to leave town and sent {D.him} money for expenses."), E(.document, 2, "Creditors", "{V} owed several people money and had threats on file."), E(.forensic, 1, "No Gun", "No gun that fired the bullet has been found.")],
        role: "Lead investigator",
        exam: [.direct("What did the bank records show?", "\"About $1.1 million moved from {V}'s accounts into {D}'s companies in two years, signed by {DL} under a power of attorney.\""), .direct("How did {V} come to hire {D}?", "\"{V} won a $9 million jackpot and hired {DL}, a self-described business manager, to handle the money.\""), .direct("What about the texts from {V}'s phone?", "\"For ten months they said {V} was traveling. They were sent from towers near {DL}'s home and share {DL}'s habit of dropping apostrophes.\""), .direct("Where was the body found?", "\"In a drainage pond, a year after {V} vanished. A landscaper clearing the pond found it.\""), .direct("What did the autopsy show?", "\"One gunshot wound to the head. A .38-caliber bullet was recovered.\""), .direct("What did divers find?", "\"A pistol cleaning kit tied to a brick near the body. Nothing else of {V}'s was recovered there.\""), .cross("Did anyone see the defendant with {V} that night?", "\"Not that night. We have no witness who saw them together near the time {V} disappeared.\""), .cross("Was a weapon linked to the defendant?", "\"Not yet. We have not found the .38, and the cleaning kit has not been tied to {D.him}.\""), .cross("Did {V} sign the power of attorney?", "\"Yes. It appears to be signed by {V}, and {DL} acted under it.\""), .cross("Did {V} have a history of traveling?", "\"After the win, yes. {V} talked about seeing the world.\""), .cross("Did anyone else have a reason to harm {V}?", "\"A few people asked for money after the win. I did not rule them out.\"")],
        defenseRole: "{V}'s former creditor",
        defenseExam: [.direct("How did you know {V}?", "\"I lent {V} money before the win, and I knew {V} from the neighborhood.\""), .direct("Did {V} owe you?", "\"Thousands. {V} borrowed from me in a rough year and said I would be paid back.\""), .direct("Did {V} pay you after the win?", "\"Part of it. {V} paid a little and said the rest would come when things settled.\""), .direct("Did you threaten {V}?", "\"We had words. I was frustrated, and I said some things I should not have.\""), .direct("Did you see {V} after the win?", "\"A few times. {V} was avoiding me, and I could not get a straight answer.\""), .direct("What did you know about {D}?", "\"I knew {V} hired {D} to manage the money. I never met {DF}.\""), .cross("What did you say in your words with {V}?", "\"That I wanted my money. I said I would not wait forever.\""), .cross("Did you ever visit the pond?", "\"No. I did not, and I would not know where it is.\""), .cross("Where were you when {V} disappeared?", "\"At work, as far as I can recall. I have records.\""), .cross("Did you own a .38?", "\"No. I have never owned a pistol.\""), .cross("Did you speak with investigators?", "\"Yes, and I gave them what I knew.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took a winner's money and killed {V} to hide it.", "A man who wanted out and had angry creditors."),
        allocution: "\"I took money I shouldn't have. I did not kill {V}.\"",
        truths: ("{DL}'s phone was at the pond the night {V} vanished.", "{V}'s creditor was seen with {V}'s truck a day after the last text."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you kill {V}?", "\"No. I did not kill {V}. I managed {V}'s money, and I had no reason to harm {V}.\""), .direct("Where did the money go?", "\"Investments. I put it in my companies, and I meant to grow it for {V}.\""), .direct("Why were the transfers signed by you?", "\"I had a power of attorney, which {V} gave me. I used it as I was permitted.\""), .direct("What about the texts?", "\"{V} asked me to send some. {V} wanted to travel quietly and not be bothered by people asking for money.\""), .direct("Why did you think {V} disappeared?", "\"{V} told me {V} wanted to leave. I believed {V} chose to disappear, and the money was a loan I meant to repay.\""), .direct("Why was {V}'s body in a pond?", "\"I do not know why. I was shocked when I learned, and I have no idea how it got there.\""), .cross("$1.1 million went to your companies, didn't it?", "\"Yes. As a loan from {V}, under the power of attorney.\""), .cross("You sent texts from {V}'s phone for ten months, didn't you?", "\"{V} asked me to, and I did. I should have told someone.\""), .cross("The texts were sent from towers near your home, weren't they?", "\"I sent them at home. That is where I live.\""), .cross("You write without apostrophes, don't you?", "\"I do, like many people. That does not make me a killer.\""), .cross("You are the only person who benefited from {V}'s disappearance, aren't you?", "\"I do not think so. Others had asked for money, and I was not the only one.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} won a $9 million jackpot and hired {D}, a self-described business manager, to handle the money. Within two years $1.1 million had moved to {D}'s companies, texts from {V}'s phone said {V} was traveling for ten months, and a landscaper found {V}'s body in a drainage pond, shot once in the head.", "{V} chose to disappear, and the money was a loan under a power of attorney {V} signed. Nothing ties {D} to a weapon, a witness, or the pond."),
        closings: ("A fortune, $1.1 million moved to {D}'s companies, ten months of false texts, and a body in a pond. The person who gained from the silence was {D}.", "A signed power of attorney, texts {V} asked for, and no weapon, no witness, and no confession. The State has a motive and a suspicion, not a killer."),
        timeline: [(-700, "{V} wins the jackpot."), (-300, "{DL} takes over {V}'s money."), (-300, "{V} vanishes; texts begin."), (0, "A landscaper finds a body in a drainage pond.")],
        identified: "A body in a drainage pond and a money trail.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .female, "V": .male])

    static let keyedCarLotV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.keyedCarLot",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Neighbor's Car Scratched in Garage Row After Dispute", "Doorbell Video Shows Person Walking Past Car"],
        law: "injuryPersonalProperty",
        threshold: 5,
        spec: "Willfully and wantonly injured personal property of {V}, a car, causing damage of $1,100, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 20...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V}'s car was scratched along the driver side in a shared garage row on {DATE}. Two days earlier, {D} and {V} had argued about a blocked bay. A doorbell camera across the row shows a person in a gray hoodie walking along the car. {DL} says {D.he} was at a night class. Damage was put at $1,100.",
        state: [E(.video, 2, "Doorbell Video", "A person in a gray hoodie drags a hand along the driver side at 9:40 p.m."), E(.document, 3, "Message", "{D} texted {V}: 'Move it or I'll move it for you.'")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Night Class", "{DL} says {D.he} was in class until 9:30.")],
        role: "Garage neighbor",
        exam: [.direct("What did the doorbell video show?", "\"A person in a gray hoodie walking along {V}'s car at 9:40 p.m., dragging a hand along the driver side.\""), .direct("Whose car was it?", "\"{V}'s. It sits in the next bay in our shared garage row. I see it every day.\""), .direct("What was the dispute?", "\"A blocked bay. {D} and {V} had argued about it two days earlier, and it got loud.\""), .direct("What damage was done?", "\"A scratch along the whole driver side. It was put at $1,100 for the repair.\""), .direct("What did {D} text {V}?", "\"'Move it or I'll move it for you.' That was sent after the argument over the bay.\""), .direct("How did {V} learn of the damage?", "\"{V} came out the next morning and saw the scratch. {V} knocked on my door and asked if I had seen anything.\""), .cross("Could you see the face?", "\"No. The hood covered it, and the video is too dark to see features.\""), .cross("Is the hoodie common?", "\"Yes. Plenty of people on this row wear a gray hoodie. I own one myself.\""), .cross("Could you tell a hand from a key?", "\"No. The person drags something along the paint. It might be a hand or a key.\""), .cross("Did you see the defendant near the car?", "\"No. I was inside. I only know from the video.\""), .cross("Did the defendant deny it?", "\"Yes. {D.He} told me flatly that {D.he} did not touch the car.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} scratched a car after a threat.", "A night class and an unseen face."),
        allocution: "\"I said something I regret. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL}'s class ended at 8:15 and {D.he} came straight home.", "{DL} stayed to help a classmate with a flat tire until 9:50."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you scratch the car?", "\"No. I did not touch {V}'s car, and I never would. I do not damage other people's property.\""), .direct("Where were you that evening?", "\"In class. I take a night class twice a week, and I was there until after nine.\""), .direct("What about the text?", "\"Heat of the moment. I was angry about the blocked bay, and I wrote something I should not have.\""), .direct("What about the hoodie?", "\"I own one. It is plain gray, like thousands of others, and I wear it to class.\""), .direct("What did you think when you heard about the scratch?", "\"I was upset. I knew the text would make me a suspect, and I was afraid.\""), .direct("What do you want {V} to know?", "\"I am sorry about the argument and about the text. I did not scratch your car.\""), .cross("You wrote 'Move it or I'll move it for you,' didn't you?", "\"Yes. It was a bad text, and I understand how it reads.\""), .cross("You and {V} argued two days before, didn't you?", "\"Yes. It was a loud argument about the bay, and I was frustrated.\""), .cross("You own a gray hoodie, don't you?", "\"Yes, and so do many people on this row.\""), .cross("You could have come home before 9:40, couldn't you?", "\"Class lets out around then. I came home after, and I did not walk by the car.\""), .cross("No one can confirm where you were, can they?", "\"A classmate might. I told the deputy the class name and time.\"")],
        openings: ("{V}'s car was scratched along the driver side in a shared garage row. Two days earlier {D} had argued with {V} about a blocked bay and texted, 'Move it or I'll move it for you,' and a doorbell camera caught a person in a gray hoodie dragging a hand along the car.", "{D} was at a night class, and the person on the video wore a common gray hoodie with the hood up. A bad text after an argument is not proof of vandalism."),
        closings: ("A blocked bay, a threatening text, and a gray hoodie dragging along {V}'s car at 9:40. The argument and the damage come from the same dispute.", "A hood that hid every feature, a hoodie half the row owns, and a class {D} was attending. The State has a text, not a face."),
        timeline: [(-2, "The argument about the bay."), (-1, "{DL} sends the text."), (0, "9:40 p.m.: the scratch."), (1, "{V} discovers the damage.")],
        identified: "A doorbell camera and a text.",
        mood: .indifferent)

    static let fuelCardMisuseV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.fuelCardMisuse",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Delivery Driver Used Company Fuel Card for Family Car", "Monthly Statement Shows Pumps Near Driver's Home"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        threshold: 5,
        spec: "Stole gasoline valued at $389 belonging to {V}, a bakery, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V}, a bakery, found 16 fuel card charges totaling $389 in one month at stations near {D}'s home, on days {D} did not deliver. The card was assigned to {D}. {DL} says {D.he} used it only for the delivery van and that the owner allowed some personal miles.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Card Statement", "16 charges totaling $389 on days off."), E(.video, 2, "Station Video", "{D} at the pump in a personal sedan.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Personal Miles", "{DL} says the owner allowed personal use.")],
        role: "Bakery owner",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find on the fuel card statement?", "\"Sixteen charges totaling $389 in one month at stations near {D}'s home, on days {DL} did not deliver.\""), .direct("Who held the card?", "\"{DL}, a delivery driver. The card was assigned to {DL} for the bakery van.\""), .direct("What does the station video show?", "\"{DL} at the pump in a personal sedan on one of those days. The van is not in the picture.\""), .direct("What are the card's rules?", "\"The card is for the bakery van. It was meant for fuel for deliveries, and I never told anyone to use it elsewhere.\""), .direct("How did you notice the charges?", "\"I reviewed the statement at month end. The stations and the days did not match the delivery schedule.\""), .direct("What did you do when you saw it?", "\"I pulled the statements and the schedule and compared them line by line. Sixteen charges stood out.\""), .cross("Did you allow personal use?", "\"Never. I did not say it was allowed, and I did not say it was banned in writing.\""), .cross("Was there a written policy?", "\"No policy either way. We are a small bakery, and we run on trust.\""), .cross("Did you tell {D} not to use it on days off?", "\"I assumed. I never said it in words, and I know I should have.\""), .cross("Did the defendant cooperate?", "\"Yes. {D.He} said some miles were personal and showed me where.\""), .cross("How much did the defendant deliver for you?", "\"A lot. {D.He} has been reliable for years, and I trust {D.him} in most things.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} fueled a personal car with the bakery's card.", "A casual arrangement."),
        allocution: "\"I should have asked. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} texted a friend, \"Free gas, finally.\"", "The owner texted {DL}, \"Fill up whatever you need.\" a month earlier."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you use the card on days off?", "\"Sometimes. I used it on days I did not deliver, for a personal car I also use for errands.\""), .direct("Why?", "\"The owner said it was fine. {V} told me to fill up whatever I needed.\""), .direct("Where is that in writing?", "\"A text. The owner texted me about a month earlier, and I kept it on my phone.\""), .direct("How many times did you do it?", "\"I lost count. I did not keep track, because I thought it was all within what the owner said.\""), .direct("Did you ever hide the charges?", "\"No. They were on the statement every month, and I never tried to hide anything.\""), .direct("What do you want the owner to know?", "\"I thought I had permission. If I was wrong, I will pay back every dollar.\""), .cross("Sixteen charges on days you did not deliver, weren't there?", "\"That is what the statement says. I did not count, and I do not dispute the number.\""), .cross("You filled up a personal sedan, didn't you?", "\"Yes, sometimes. I thought it was allowed.\""), .cross("The owner says there was never permission, doesn't the owner?", "\"The owner says so now. I have the text, and I think it says otherwise.\""), .cross("You never asked again before using it, did you?", "\"No. I did not ask each time, and I should have.\""), .cross("$389 is a lot for personal use, isn't it?", "\"It is. I would not have used it so often if I thought it was wrong.\"")],
        openings: ("A bakery found 16 fuel card charges totaling $389 in one month at stations near {D}'s home, on days {D} did not deliver. The card was assigned to {D}, and a station camera shows {D} at the pump in a personal sedan.", "The owner told {D} to fill up whatever was needed, and {D} did exactly that. Small-bakery trust with no written policy is not a theft."),
        closings: ("Sixteen charges on days off, a personal sedan at the pump, and a card for the bakery van. {D} used company fuel for personal driving.", "A text from the owner, no written policy, and charges that sat in plain view on every statement. The State must prove {D} knew the use was not allowed."),
        timeline: [(-30, "The month begins."), (-5, "The statement arrives."), (0, "{V} confronts {DL}.")],
        identified: "A fuel card statement.",
        mood: .wantsConviction)

    static let dogfightingRingV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.dogfightingRing",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Scarred Dogs and a Pit Found Behind Pine Grove Barn", "Owner Says the Dogs Were Hunting Hounds"],
        law: "animalCruelty",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Maliciously tortured, mutilated, and cruelly killed animals, by keeping and training dogs for fighting and causing them to fight, on and before {DATE}.",
        ages: 30...55,
        victim: false,
        summary: "After a neighbor's tip about nighttime crowds, deputies and animal services searched {D}'s barn property with a warrant on {DATE}. They found eleven scarred pit bull-type dogs tied to buried tires, a plywood pit with blood stains, a scale, and a bag of injectable drugs. Two dogs were buried nearby. {DL} says the dogs are hunting hounds, the pit was a training ring for obedience, and a renter used the barn at night.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Plywood Pit", "A carpeted plywood pit with old blood in the corners, a scale, and a leash bundle.", .search), E(.document, 3, "Fight Log", "A notebook of dog weights, dates, and entries like 'W 41 lbs, lost 2nd.'", .search), E(.forensic, 2, "Necropsy", "Both buried dogs died of bite wounds to the head within days.")],
        defense: [E(.document, 2, "Rental Note", "A handwritten note renting the barn to a man on weekends."), E(.statement, 1, "Training", "{DL} says the pit was for obedience work.")],
        role: "Animal services supervisor",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find at the property?", "\"Eleven scarred dogs tied to buried tires, a carpeted plywood pit with old blood in the corners, a scale, and a bag of injectable drugs.\""), .direct("What explained the scars?", "\"Consistent with fights, with scarring to the face and forelegs. The patterns are typical of dogs that have been matched.\""), .direct("What was in the notebook?", "\"A log of dog weights, dates, and entries like 'W 41 lbs, lost 2nd.' It reads like a record of matches.\""), .direct("What did the necropsy show on the buried dogs?", "\"Both died of bite wounds to the head within days of burial. They were buried near the barn.\""), .direct("How did the investigation start?", "\"A neighbor reported nighttime crowds at the barn property. We watched, then obtained a warrant.\""), .direct("What condition were the living dogs in?", "\"Thin, scarred, and tied short to tires. Several had untreated wounds, and all were taken into protective custody.\""), .cross("Do hunting dogs scar?", "\"Sometimes. Hunting dogs get cut by brush and animals. The scars on these dogs were not like that.\""), .cross("Was a rental of the barn proven?", "\"A note, nothing more. We found a note referring to a renter, and no lease.\""), .cross("Did anyone see a fight?", "\"No. We found the setup and the evidence. We did not see dogs fighting while we were there.\""), .cross("Whose handwriting is in the log?", "\"We have not determined that. We are examining it.\""), .cross("Did {D} cooperate?", "\"{D} answered questions and said the barn had a renter at night. {D.He} did not resist.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Hunting club member",
        defenseExam: [.direct("How do you know {D}?", "\"We are in the same hunting club. I have known {D} for years and hunted with {D.his} family.\""), .direct("Did the defendant run hunting dogs?", "\"A couple of hounds, years back. They were good dogs, and {DF} treated them well.\""), .direct("What are hunting hounds like?", "\"Lean, long-eared, and bred to track. They are very different from the dogs found in the barn.\""), .direct("Did you ever see a pit at the defendant's property?", "\"Not until now. I was never invited into the barn, and I did not see anything like that.\""), .direct("Did you hear talk of fights?", "\"Never. Nothing in our club or at {D.his} place ever suggested dogs were fought.\""), .direct("What is the defendant's reputation?", "\"A fair hunter and a decent neighbor. {D.He} would not have been the first to come to mind for this.\""), .cross("Were you at the barn at night?", "\"No. I only visited during the day, and I did not go into the barn.\""), .cross("Do you know who rented the barn?", "\"No. I did not know anyone rented it.\""), .cross("Have you seen the dogs in the barn?", "\"No. I only know what I heard from the sheriff.\""), .cross("Are hunting dogs ever kept on tires?", "\"Sometimes. People chain dogs to stakes or tires to keep them from running.\""), .cross("Are you protecting the defendant?", "\"I only know what I saw at the barn, and I gain nothing either way.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} bred and fought dogs on {D.his} property.", "Hunting dogs, an obedience ring, and a renter."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry for what those animals went through.\"",
        truths: ("{DL}'s phone has texts about 'matches' and weights.", "The renter's name is in {DL}'s phone, and the log is in the renter's handwriting."),
        defendant: [.direct("Whose dogs were they?", "\"Mine, but I do not fight them. They are working and training dogs, and I do not breed them to fight.\""), .direct("What was the plywood pit?", "\"A training ring. I used it for obedience and for socializing the dogs in a closed space.\""), .direct("What about the scars?", "\"Fights when they got loose. Some of them got into scraps in the yard, and I never treated them well enough.\""), .direct("What about the scale?", "\"I weigh my dogs for food and medicine. A scale is a simple tool, and it does not mean I fought them.\""), .direct("What about the injectable drugs?", "\"Vitamins and antibiotics, which I gave to the dogs myself. I should have used a vet.\""), .direct("What about the log?", "\"Not my writing. A renter used the barn at night, and I did not go in then.\""), .cross("The pit had old blood in the corners, didn't it?", "\"Dogs bleed when they scrap in a yard. I did not think about cleaning it.\""), .cross("Two dogs were buried near the barn, weren't they?", "\"Yes. They died of injuries, and I buried them. I should have taken them to a vet.\""), .cross("A notebook recorded weights and 'lost 2nd,' didn't it?", "\"I did not write it. I do not know what it means.\""), .cross("You cannot produce the renter, can you?", "\"I have a first name and a number that no longer works. I told investigators.\""), .cross("Eleven scarred dogs were on your property, weren't they?", "\"Yes. They are mine, and I take responsibility for their condition.\"")],
        openings: ("After a neighbor's tip about nighttime crowds, deputies and animal services searched {D}'s barn property and found eleven scarred pit bull-type dogs tied to buried tires, a plywood pit with old blood, a scale, a fight log, and two dead dogs buried nearby.", "The dogs are working animals, the pit was a training ring, and a renter used the barn at night. A property that is searched is not proof that its owner fought dogs."),
        closings: ("Eleven scarred dogs, a bloodstained pit, a scale, a log of weights and matches, and two buried dogs. Every detail points to a fighting operation on {D}'s property.", "A renter at night, handwriting that is not {D}'s, and no one who saw a fight. The State must prove {D} ran this operation, and {D} says someone else did."),
        timeline: [(-30, "A neighbor reports crowds at night."), (-7, "Deputies drive by and hear dogs."), (0, "Morning: the warrant is served."), (0, "Noon: dogs seized.")],
        identified: "A neighbor's tip.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["searchSeizure", "burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let parkingLotSleeperV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.parkingLotSleeper",
        category: .traffic,
        headlines: ["Man Found Slumped at Wheel of Idling Truck Behind Closed Church", "Was the Truck Driven, or Only Parked?"],
        law: "habitualDWI",
        threshold: 2,
        spec: "Drove a vehicle while impaired, having three prior DWI convictions within ten years.",
        ages: 35...58,
        victim: false,
        summary: "At about 1:40 a.m. on {DATE}, a deputy found {D} slumped in the driver's seat of an idling pickup in the back lot of a closed church, keys in the ignition, lights off, transmission in park. {DL} blew 0.15. {DL} has three DWI convictions in the last nine years, so this is a felony if {D.he} was \"driving.\" {DL} says a friend drove the truck there from a party and left, and that {D.he} was only waiting for a ride.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Breath Test", "Intoxilyzer result of 0.15 at 2:25 a.m."), E(.video, 2, "Party Lot Camera", "A pickup like {DL}'s leaves a house party lot at 12:55 a.m.; the driver cannot be seen."), E(.document, 2, "Prior Convictions", "Three DWI convictions in the past nine years.")],
        defense: [E(.digital, 3, "Friend's Text", "A text at 1:05 a.m. from a friend: \"Parked you at the church. Your keys are in the ignition. Ride soon.\""), E(.statement, 2, "No Observed Driving", "No one saw the truck move after it stopped at the church."), E(.video, 1, "Church Camera", "The church camera was dark that night.")],
        role: "Patrol deputy",
        exam: [.direct("Describe your work as a patrol deputy.", "\"I patrol the county at night, check parking lots and closed businesses, and respond to impaired driving calls. I have handled many stops for drivers who were drinking.\""), .direct("Where did you find {D} at about 1:40 a.m. on {DATE}?", "\"In the back lot of a closed church, slumped in the driver's seat of an idling pickup. The keys were in the ignition, the lights were off, and the transmission was in park.\""), .direct("What was the defendant's condition?", "\"{D} had slurred speech, red eyes, and a strong smell of liquor. {D.He} was hard to wake at first, and I had to speak loudly and tap the window.\""), .direct("What did the breath test show?", "\"An Intoxilyzer result of 0.15 at 2:25 a.m. That is nearly twice the legal limit, and it was taken at the station after the arrest.\""), .direct("What did you learn about the defendant's record?", "\"{D.He} has three DWI convictions in the past nine years. A fourth is a felony if {D.he} was driving, so the question here is whether {D.he} drove.\""), .direct("What did the party lot camera show?", "\"A pickup like {D.his} leaving a house party lot at 12:55 a.m. The driver cannot be seen, and I do not know who was behind the wheel.\""), .cross("Did you see the truck move?", "\"No. I never saw the truck move. It was parked, idling, with the lights off when I found it.\""), .cross("Did anyone see the defendant drive?", "\"No one has told me they saw {DL} drive. The church camera was dark that night, and no witness saw the truck after it stopped.\""), .cross("Was there a text on the defendant's phone about the truck?", "\"A friend's text at 1:05 a.m. said, Parked you at the church. Your keys are in the ignition. Ride soon. {D.He} had deleted it before I asked for the phone.\""), .cross("Did the friend later say who drove?", "\"Yes. The friend later admitted driving and parking the truck at the church. I did not know that when I made the arrest.\""), .cross("Was it warm in the truck when you found it?", "\"The engine was running, and the heater was on. It was a humid night, and I could not tell how long the truck had been parked.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Party host",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Tell us how you know {D}.", "\"I hosted the house party that night. {D} is a friend I have known for years, and I saw {DF} arrive and leave.\""), .direct("What did you see the defendant do at the party?", "\"{DF} was drinking and was unsteady by midnight. I told {DF} not to drive, and {DF} said a friend would take care of it.\""), .direct("Did the defendant drive away from your house?", "\"No. A friend of {DF}'s took the keys and drove the truck out of my lot. I saw the truck leave around 12:55 in the morning.\""), .direct("Who was the friend who took the keys?", "\"I did not see clearly. It was dark, and several people were leaving. I only saw someone take the keys from {DF} and get behind the wheel.\""), .direct("How did the defendant seem when the truck left?", "\"Out of it. {DF} could barely stand, and {DF} climbed into the passenger side, and I thought someone was taking {DF} home.\""), .direct("What did you do after the truck left?", "\"I went back inside and cleaned up. I did not think anything of it until I heard that {D.he} had been found at the church.\""), .cross("Did you see the driver's face?", "\"No. I did not. I saw a person take the keys, but it was dark, and I could not say who it was.\""), .cross("Did you see which friend took the keys?", "\"Not clearly. I only know it was one of {D.his} friends. I cannot name the person, and I did not see where the truck went.\""), .cross("Did you see the defendant drive any time that night?", "\"No. I did not see {DF} drive. I saw {DF} get into the passenger side, but I did not see {DF} again after that.\""), .cross("Did you hear about the church lot?", "\"Only afterward. I did not know the truck had gone to the church until a deputy asked me about the party.\""), .cross("Did you stop {D} from taking the truck?", "\"I tried to talk {DF} out of driving. I thought someone else was driving, so I did not push harder, and I regret that.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} drove drunk and stopped at a church.", "A friend drove and left, and {D} only waited."),
        allocution: "\"I made a bad choice again. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} deleted the friend's text from the phone before the deputy asked for it.", "The friend later admitted driving and parking the truck at the church."),
        defendant: [.direct("Please describe your night at the house party.", "\"I went to a house party with friends and drank too much. I knew I was in no condition to drive, and I planned to get a ride home.\""), .direct("Did you drive the truck to the church?", "\"No. A friend drove the truck from the party and parked it at the church. I was in the passenger seat, and I do not remember much of the ride.\""), .direct("Why were you sitting in the driver's seat?", "\"I moved over to wait for my ride. I sat behind the wheel because the seat was comfortable, and I did not think about how it would look.\""), .direct("Why were the keys in the ignition?", "\"The friend left them there when the friend got out. I did not take them out, and I did not start the truck again.\""), .direct("What did you do with the friend's text?", "\"I deleted it before the deputy asked for the phone. I was scared and ashamed, and I know deleting it was a mistake.\""), .direct("What was the plan after the friend parked the truck?", "\"The friend said a ride was coming soon. I stayed in the truck and waited, and I fell asleep before anyone arrived.\""), .cross("You have three DWI convictions, don't you?", "\"Yes. I know what happens if I am found driving again. That is why I did not drive, and why I waited for a ride.\""), .cross("You blew a 0.15, didn't you?", "\"Yes. That is what the test showed. I was very drunk, and I knew better than to drive.\""), .cross("You deleted the friend's text before the deputy asked for it, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I deleted it. I panicked, and I know it looks like I was hiding something.\""), .cross("The engine was running, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. The heater was on. The friend left it running when the friend got out, and I did not turn it off.\""), .cross("No one else was in the truck when the deputy found you, were they?", "\"No. I was alone. The friend had already left, and I have no one at the church who can confirm what I say.\"")],
        openings: ("At about 1:40 a.m. on {DATE}, a deputy found {D} slumped in the driver's seat of an idling pickup in the back lot of a closed church. The keys were in the ignition, and {D} blew 0.15, with three prior DWI convictions.", "The defense will present a friend's text that said Parked you at the church, a party host who saw someone else take the keys, and a friend who later admitted driving. No one saw {D} drive."),
        closings: ("A drunk driver at the wheel of a running truck, keys in the ignition, a breath test of 0.15, and three DWI convictions. {D} deleted the text that explained how the truck got there.", "A friend's text and a waiting ride, a party host who saw someone else take the keys, and a friend who admitted driving. No one saw {D} drive, and the State has not proved otherwise."),
        timeline: [(0, "12:55 a.m.: a pickup leaves the party lot."), (0, "1:05 a.m.: the friend texts {DL}."), (0, "1:40 a.m.: the deputy finds {DL}."), (0, "2:25 a.m.: the breath test.")],
        identified: "A deputy on patrol.",
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let grandparentHouseV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.grandparentHouse",
        category: .drugs,
        headlines: ["Postal Inspectors Flag Parcels to a Retiree's Address; Pills Found in Basement", "Grandparent Says Parcels Were Grandson's Online Orders"],
        law: "maintainingDwelling",
        threshold: 6,
        spec: "Knowingly kept or maintained a dwelling that was resorted to by persons using or selling controlled substances.",
        ages: 71...78,
        victim: false,
        summary: "After postal inspectors flagged parcels sent to {D}'s address, deputies searched the house with a warrant on {DATE}. In the finished basement where {D}'s grandson lived, they found 120 counterfeit pills, a pill press, and $2,400. Seven of the parcel labels were signed for in {D}'s name. {DL} says {D.he} signed because the grandson said they were car parts and never went downstairs.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Parcel Log", "Nine parcels to the house over six weeks; seven signed with {DL}'s name."), E(.physical, 3, "Basement Pill Press", "A pill press, dies, and 120 pills with a stamp mark in the basement."), E(.statement, 2, "Neighbor Complaint", "A neighbor says {DL} was told about late-night visitors and said, \"It's family business.\"")],
        defense: [E(.document, 2, "Basement Lock", "The basement door has a deadbolt and a key only the grandson held."), E(.document, 2, "Medical Records", "{DL} has severe hip pain and a heart condition and rarely uses stairs."), E(.statement, 1, "Grandson's Plea", "The grandson pleaded guilty and said {DL} knew nothing about the press.")],
        role: "Postal inspector",
        exam: [.direct("What do you do as a postal inspector?", "\"I investigate crimes involving the mail, including drug shipments. I track parcels, review delivery logs, and work with deputies to obtain warrants.\""), .direct("What did you notice about parcels sent to {D}'s address?", "\"Nine parcels from overseas arrived over six weeks, all addressed to {D}'s house. That pattern prompted me to look more closely.\""), .direct("Who signed for the parcels?", "\"Seven of the parcel labels were signed with {D.his} name. The other two were left at the door, according to the delivery log.\""), .direct("What did deputies find in the basement?", "\"120 counterfeit pills with a stamp mark, a pill press, dies, and $2,400. The basement was where {D.his} grandchild lived.\""), .direct("How was the basement secured?", "\"The door had a deadbolt, and the key was held only by the grandchild. {D.He} did not have a key to the basement.\""), .direct("What did neighbors say?", "\"A neighbor said {DL} was told about late-night visitors and said, It's family business. I considered that statement along with the rest.\""), .cross("Did the defendant order anything that was delivered?", "\"I found no record that {D.he} ordered anything. The parcels came to the house, and the orders were tied to the grandchild.\""), .cross("Did the parcel labels say what was inside?", "\"They said car parts. I do not know whether {D.he} looked at the labels, and I do not know what {D.he} understood.\""), .cross("What did the grandchild say after the arrest?", "\"The grandchild pleaded guilty and said {D.he} knew nothing about the press. That statement matters, and I considered it carefully.\""), .cross("Did the defendant have physical limits that affect going downstairs?", "\"Yes. Medical records show severe hip pain and a heart condition. {D.He} rarely uses stairs, and the basement stairs are steep.\""), .cross("Did you find evidence the defendant knew what was in the boxes?", "\"Some evidence. {DL} once helped repackage a box and said, Don't tell anybody what's in these. I cannot say what {DL} understood by that.\"")],
        defenseRole: "{DL}'s home health nurse",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What does your work as a home health nurse involve?", "\"I visit {D}'s home several times a week. I check {D.his} heart condition, help with hip pain, and make sure medications are taken.\""), .direct("What can {D} do physically?", "\"Very little on stairs. {DF} has severe hip pain and a heart condition, and I have never seen {DF} go down to the basement.\""), .direct("What do you see when you visit the house?", "\"I see the main floor and the landing at the top of the basement stairs. The basement door is kept shut with a deadbolt.\""), .direct("How would you describe the defendant's relationship with the grandchild?", "\"Trusting and loving. {DF} believes what the grandchild says, and I have heard {DF} defend the grandchild many times.\""), .direct("Did you see any sign of drug activity at the house?", "\"No. I never saw pills, scales, or anything unusual in the rooms I visit. I did not hear anything suspicious.\""), .direct("What did you think when you learned about the basement?", "\"I was shocked. I could not believe what was down there, and I told the deputies that {D.he} never went down the stairs.\""), .cross("Do you see the basement?", "\"Only from the landing. I have never gone down, and I do not know what was kept there.\""), .cross("Did you ever see the defendant sign for parcels?", "\"Once or twice. I saw {DF} sign for a box at the door. I did not look at the label or ask what was in it.\""), .cross("Did the defendant ever mention visitors at night?", "\"No. {DF} did not mention them to me. I come during the day, and I do not know who visited at night.\""), .cross("Could the defendant have gone downstairs without your knowing?", "\"Possibly. I am not there all day. But with {D.his} hip and heart, I think it would be very difficult.\""), .cross("Did you know about the box that {D} helped repackage?", "\"No. I did not know about that until the case. I only know what I saw during my visits.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} signed for parcels and kept a house used for drugs.", "A frail grandparent who signed for packages and never went downstairs."),
        allocution: "\"I should have asked more questions about those boxes.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} once helped repackage a box and said, \"Don't tell anybody what's in these.\"", "The grandson told friends that his grandparent \"believes anything I say.\""),
        defendant: [.direct("Tell us about your life with your grandchild.", "\"My grandchild lived in the finished basement. I love my grandchild and I let the grandchild stay, and I did not ask many questions about the grandchild's life.\""), .direct("Why did you sign for parcels?", "\"The mail carrier asked me to sign. My grandchild told me they were car parts, and I believed my grandchild. I thought I was helping.\""), .direct("Have you gone to the basement?", "\"Not in years. The stairs are steep, and my hip and my heart make it hard. My grandchild kept it locked, and I never had a key.\""), .direct("What did you think about the visitors at night?", "\"I thought they were the grandchild's friends. I told a neighbor it was family business because I did not want to gossip about my grandchild.\""), .direct("What did you say when you helped repackage a box?", "\"I said not to tell anyone what was in the box. I thought it was a surprise gift. I did not know it was anything illegal.\""), .direct("What do you say now about what your grandchild did?", "\"I am heartbroken. I trusted my grandchild, and I did not know. I did not know about the pills or the press until deputies came.\""), .cross("Seven parcels were signed in your name, weren't they?", "\"Yes. I signed them. The mail carrier handed me a pad, and I wrote my name. I did not read what was on the labels.\""), .cross("You told a neighbor it was family business, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I said that about the visitors. I was protecting my grandchild's privacy, and I know how it sounds now.\""), .cross("You helped repackage a box once, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I helped close a box that my grandchild was sending. I did not look inside, and I did not know what was in it.\""), .cross("Your grandchild told friends you believe anything the grandchild says, didn't the grandchild?", "\"I do not know what the grandchild told friends. I know I trust my grandchild. I know that may have been foolish, and I regret it a lot.\""), .cross("You never asked what was in the parcels, did you?", "\"No. I did not. I trusted my grandchild. I know that I should have asked more, and I did not.\"")],
        openings: ("After postal inspectors flagged nine parcels sent to {D}'s address, deputies found 120 counterfeit pills, a pill press, and $2,400 in the basement where {D}'s grandchild lived. Seven parcel labels were signed in {D}'s name.", "The defense will present a frail grandparent who signed for packages because the grandchild said they were car parts, who never went downstairs, and a grandchild who pleaded guilty and said {D} knew nothing."),
        closings: ("Nine parcels in six weeks, seven signed in {D}'s name, a neighbor told it was family business, and a box repackaged with a warning not to tell anyone what was in it. The signatures are {D}'s.", "A locked basement with a deadbolt, a grandchild who held the only key and pleaded guilty, and a grandparent too frail for the stairs. The State has not proved that {D} knew what was downstairs."),
        timeline: [(-42, "The first parcel arrives."), (-14, "A neighbor mentions the visitors."), (-3, "Inspectors flag the parcels."), (0, "The warrant is served.")],
        identified: "Postal inspectors flagged parcels.",
        mood: .sympathetic,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .female])

    static let birthdayPartyV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.birthdayParty",
        category: .robbery,
        headlines: ["Tracking Tag Found Under Car Bumper of Woman With Protective Order", "Ex-Husband's App Account Tied to Hidden GPS Tag"],
        law: "stalkingCourtOrder",
        threshold: 6,
        spec: "On more than one occasion followed, was in the presence of, and watched {V} without legal purpose while a domestic violence protective order prohibiting that conduct was in effect, causing {V} to fear for {V.his} safety, between September and {DATE}.",
        ages: 26...45,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V} has a one-year protective order against {D}, {V.his} ex-husband, ordering {D.him} to stay 300 feet away except for custody exchanges. On {DATE}, a mechanic changing {V}'s oil found a GPS tag taped inside the rear bumper. The tag's account was registered to an email address of {D}'s. A camera at {V}'s gym had also shown {D}'s truck idling outside twice that month. {DL} says the tag was an old one for {D.his} tool trailer and the truck was on {D.his} route to work.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "GPS Tag", "A small tag taped inside the bumper, linked to an account under {D}'s email."), E(.video, 3, "Gym Camera", "{D}'s truck idles across from the gym entrance for 25 minutes on two mornings."), E(.document, 2, "Protective Order", "A one-year DVPO: stay 300 feet from {V} and {V}'s home, work, and gym.")],
        defense: [E(.document, 2, "Tool Trailer", "{DL} owns a tool trailer and an old tag registered to the same account."), E(.document, 1, "Work Route", "{DL}'s work route passes the gym street.")],
        role: "Responding deputy",
        exam: [.direct("What do you do as a responding deputy?", "\"I respond to domestic violence calls and protective order violations. I take reports, collect evidence, and work with victims and prosecutors on cases like this.\""), .direct("What protective order is in place?", "\"{V} has a one-year protective order against {D}, ordering {DL} to stay 300 feet away from {V} and {V}'s home, work, and gym, except for custody exchanges.\""), .direct("What did the mechanic find on {DATE}?", "\"While changing {V}'s oil, a mechanic found a small GPS tag taped inside the rear bumper. The mechanic called {V}, and {V} called us.\""), .direct("How did you tie the tag to {D}?", "\"The tag's account was registered to an email address of {DL}'s. The account logged location checks every morning at {V}'s gym.\""), .direct("What did the gym camera show?", "\"{D.his} truck idling across from the gym entrance for 25 minutes on two mornings that month. That is within the distance the order prohibits.\""), .direct("What did {V} tell you about how this affected {V}?", "\"{V} said {V} felt watched everywhere. {V} began changing routes and gym times, and {V} did not feel safe even at home.\""), .cross("Did anyone see the defendant place the tag?", "\"No. No witness saw it placed. We only have the account records and the camera, and I cannot say who attached the tag.\""), .cross("Does the defendant's work route pass the gym?", "\"It does. The route passes the gym street, so {D.his} truck could be there for work. I cannot say that it was only for work.\""), .cross("Did the defendant own an old tag registered to the same account?", "\"Yes. {D.He} owns a tool trailer and an old tag registered to the same account. I do not know when that tag was last used.\""), .cross("Did a friend have access to the tag?", "\"{DL} says a friend with a key took it from a box in the trailer. We have not identified the friend.\""), .cross("Did the defendant approach {V} in person?", "\"I am not aware of that. The evidence is the tag and the truck, and I have no report of {DL} speaking to {V}.\"")],
        defenseRole: "{DL}'s coworker",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Walk us through how you know {D}.", "\"I am a coworker of {D}'s. We drive similar routes, and I see {D.him} at the shop every morning before the first stop.\""), .direct("What is the defendant's route?", "\"Down the street where the gym is, every morning. It is the fastest way to the first job, and everyone on the crew takes it.\""), .direct("Does the defendant stop on that street?", "\"Sometimes for coffee. There is a shop near the gym, and {D.he} stops there when the day is slow or the traffic is heavy.\""), .direct("What did you hear the defendant say about the protective order?", "\"{DF} said {DF} would follow it. {DF} was careful about custody exchanges, and I never heard {DF} threaten or complain about {V}.\""), .direct("What do you know about the defendant's tool trailer?", "\"It has tools and a box of old gear. Several people have keys, because we share equipment, and tags and tools get moved around.\""), .direct("How would you describe {D} as a coworker?", "\"Reliable and steady. {DF} never mentioned tracking anyone, and I was surprised when I heard about the tag.\""), .cross("Did you ever see the defendant outside the gym?", "\"No. I never saw {D.him} outside the gym. I only know {D.his} route, and I do not know what {D.he} did on a given morning.\""), .cross("Do you have a key to the trailer?", "\"Yes. Several of us do. I did not take the tag, and I do not know who might have.\""), .cross("Did the defendant tell you about the tag?", "\"No. {D.He} did not mention it before the case. I learned about it when the deputies came.\""), .cross("Does the route always pass the gym street?", "\"Yes. It always does. But the stop at the gym entrance for 25 minutes is not normal, and I cannot explain it.\""), .cross("Could the defendant have used the tag account?", "\"I do not know. I do not know much about the account, and I only know {D.he} had an old one in the trailer.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} tracked and watched {V} despite a court order.", "An old tag, a work route, and coincidence."),
        allocution: "\"I broke the order. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL}'s account logged the tag's location checks every morning at {V}'s gym.", "The tag had been in a box in the trailer, and a friend with a key took it."),
        defendant: [.direct("Please describe your life since the protective order.", "\"I understand the order and I try to follow it. I see my child at custody exchanges, and I work long hours on a route that crosses town.\""), .direct("Whose tag was taped under the bumper?", "\"It was an old one of mine from my tool trailer. I did not put it on {V}'s car, and I do not know how it got there.\""), .direct("Why was your truck outside the gym?", "\"It is on my route to work. I stop for coffee on that street in the morning, and I did not know {V} was inside.\""), .direct("What do you say about the location checks every morning?", "\"I do not remember making them. The tag was in a box in the trailer, and a friend with a key may have taken it.\""), .direct("How are you coping with what happened?", "\"I know why it was issued. I do not agree with everything, but I try to follow it. I would not track {V} and risk losing my child.\""), .direct("What would you tell the jury about your route?", "\"It passes the gym street. I drive it every morning at about the same time. It is a normal route, and I did not choose it to watch anyone.\""), .cross("You knew about the protective order, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I knew. I knew I had to stay 300 feet away, and I thought I was complying.\""), .cross("Your truck idled outside the gym for 25 minutes twice, didn't it?", "\"Yes. I stopped for coffee. I know it was long, and I know it looks bad, but I was not watching {V}.\""), .cross("The tag's account is under your email, isn't it?", "\"Yes. It is an old account from my trailer. I did not check it, and someone else may have used it.\""), .cross("The account logged location checks every morning, didn't it?", "\"That is what the records say. I did not run them, and I do not know who did.\""), .cross("The friend who took the tag has no name, does the friend?", "\"I do not have a name I can give you. I should have said it sooner, and I know that makes my story weak.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} has a one-year protective order against {D}. A mechanic changing {V}'s oil found a GPS tag taped inside the rear bumper, linked to an account under {D}'s email, and {D}'s truck idled outside {V}'s gym on two mornings.", "The defense will present an old tool-trailer tag that a friend with a key could have taken, and a work route that passes the gym street. A route to work is not a plan to track."),
        closings: ("A hidden tag, an account under {D}'s email that checked the location every morning at {V}'s gym, and a truck idling outside for 25 minutes twice. {D} knew the order, and the order was violated.", "An old tool tag taken by a friend with a key, and a route to work that passes the gym street. The State has not proved that {D} placed the tag or that {D} watched {V}."),
        timeline: [(-120, "The protective order begins."), (-18, "{D}'s truck at the gym."), (-9, "{D}'s truck at the gym again."), (0, "The mechanic finds the tag.")],
        identified: "A mechanic and an app account.",
        mood: .divided,
        impact: "I check my car before I get in now.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "victimRights"],
        genders: ["D": .male, "V": .female])

    static let babysitterInjuryV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.babysitterInjury",
        category: .family,
        headlines: ["Nanny Camera Shows Shaking of Infant Before Seizure", "Choking or Abuse? Nanny Charged After Baby's Brain Bleed"],
        law: "felonyChildAbuse",
        threshold: 2,
        spec: "Intentionally inflicted serious physical injury on an infant by violent shaking.",
        ages: 26...40,
        victim: false,
        summary: "{D} was a nanny hired by the parents of a five-month-old baby. On {DATE}, the nanny camera in the nursery recorded {DL} lifting the baby and shaking for about seven seconds. The baby then went limp. A hospital found bleeding under the skull and in both eyes. The baby survived with seizures. {DL} says the baby was choking on a bottle and {D.he} shook the baby to clear the airway, as {D.he} was trained.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Nanny Camera", "{DL} lifts the baby and shakes for several seconds; the baby goes limp."), E(.forensic, 3, "Pediatrician's Report", "Subdural bleeding and retinal hemorrhages typical of abusive head trauma."), E(.statement, 2, "911 Call", "{DL} told dispatch, \"The baby stopped breathing out of nowhere.\"")],
        defense: [E(.forensic, 2, "Defense Pediatrician", "Spit-up in the airway and a history of reflux could explain choking before the shake."), E(.document, 2, "CPR Certificate", "{DL} took an infant first-aid class a month earlier."), E(.document, 1, "Character", "Six years of glowing references.")],
        role: "Child abuse pediatrician",
        exam: [.direct("Describe your work as a child abuse pediatrician.", "\"I examine children who may have been abused, review imaging and medical records, and testify about whether injuries fit the reported history.\""), .direct("What injuries did you find in the baby?", "\"Bleeding under the skull and retinal hemorrhages in both eyes. The pattern is typical of abusive head trauma, and the baby survived with seizures.\""), .direct("What causes those injuries?", "\"Violent shaking or severe impact. The brain moves inside the skull, and the vessels tear. A short fall or ordinary handling does not cause this.\""), .direct("What did the nanny camera show?", "\"The nanny lifting the baby and shaking for about seven seconds. The baby then went limp, and the nanny called 911 three minutes later.\""), .direct("What did the audio capture before the shake?", "\"The nanny yelling at the baby to stop crying before the shake. The audio also captures the baby gagging and gasping before the lift.\""), .direct("What did {D} tell the 911 dispatcher?", "\"The baby stopped breathing out of nowhere. That statement does not match the video, where the baby was gagging before and the shake came after.\""), .cross("Could choking cause any of these injuries?", "\"Choking alone would not cause bleeding under the skull and in both eyes. But a forceful rescue maneuver on a choking infant could.\""), .cross("Was the baby gagging before the shake?", "\"Yes. The audio captures gagging and gasping before the lift. I cannot say whether the airway was blocked or the baby was crying.\""), .cross("Did the defendant take an infant first-aid class?", "\"Yes. {D} took a class a month earlier. The class teaches back blows and chest thrusts for choking, not shaking.\""), .cross("Does the defendant have a history with the family?", "\"Six years of glowing references. I did not find any prior complaints or injuries in the record.\""), .cross("Could reflux or spit-up explain choking?", "\"Yes. A history of reflux and spit-up in the airway could explain choking. That is possible, and I cannot rule it out.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Pediatric critical care physician",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Please describe your work in pediatric critical care.", "\"I treat critically ill infants and children in the intensive care unit. I see choking, seizures, and head injuries, and I review how they happen.\""), .direct("Can choking cause bleeding inside the head?", "\"A prolonged lack of oxygen can cause brain injury. And a forceful maneuver on a limp infant could contribute to bleeding in the head.\""), .direct("What does the audio suggest about the baby before the shake?", "\"The baby was gagging and gasping before the lift. That suggests an airway problem before any shake, which fits a choking emergency.\""), .direct("Could reflux explain the choking?", "\"Yes. A history of reflux and spit-up in the airway could explain it. Babies with reflux can choke during or after a bottle.\""), .direct("What would be a better response to a choking infant?", "\"Back blows and chest thrusts, as taught. A shake is not recommended, and it can cause injury. But panic can lead to mistakes.\""), .direct("Does the nanny's history matter to your opinion?", "\"It matters. Six years of glowing references and no prior injuries are consistent with a rescue attempt in panic, not with long abuse.\""), .cross("Can choking and a rescue maneuver cause this?", "\"A forceful maneuver on a limp infant could, in theory. But the findings here are typical of abusive head trauma.\""), .cross("Is shaking recommended?", "\"No. Back blows are taught. Shaking can cause serious injury, and no training course recommends it.\""), .cross("Did you examine the baby?", "\"I reviewed the records and imaging. I did not examine the baby myself, so I rely on the other physicians' findings.\""), .cross("Can you say what caused the bleeding?", "\"I cannot say for certain. It is consistent with shaking or severe impact, and I cannot rule out the shake.\""), .cross("Does yelling to stop crying matter to your opinion?", "\"It is relevant to what happened before. It does not tell me whether the baby was choking, but it shows frustration.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} shook an infant until the baby went limp.", "A choking emergency and a rescue gone wrong."),
        allocution: "\"I would never hurt the baby on purpose. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("The camera audio shows {DL} yelling at the baby to \"stop crying\" before the shake.", "The audio captures the baby gagging and gasping before the lift."),
        defendant: [.direct("Walk the jury through your work as a nanny.", "\"I have cared for children for six years. I have glowing references, and I have never had a complaint. I love this baby and the family.\""), .direct("What happened on the morning of the incident?", "\"The parents left for work. The baby was gagging on a bottle and started to choke. I panicked and did what I thought would clear the airway.\""), .direct("Why did you shake the baby?", "\"I thought it would clear the airway. I was scared and I did not think. I should have used back blows, as I was taught.\""), .direct("What did you do after the baby went limp?", "\"I called 911 right away. I told dispatch the baby stopped breathing, and I tried to help until paramedics arrived.\""), .direct("What training did you have?", "\"I took an infant first-aid class a month earlier. I remember some of it, but I forgot the back blows in the moment.\""), .direct("How has this affected you?", "\"I am horrible. I love this baby, and I would never hurt anyone. I think about it every day, and I wish I had done it differently.\""), .cross("You were yelling at the baby to stop crying before the shake, weren't you?", "\"Yes. I was frustrated and I yelled. I was not proud of it. Then the baby started gagging, and I panicked.\""), .cross("You were trained for choking, weren't you?", "\"Yes. I took the class a month earlier. I know back blows are taught. I forgot in the panic.\""), .cross("The video shows you shaking for about seven seconds, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. I did not count. It felt shorter, but I know the video shows what it shows.\""), .cross("You told 911 the baby stopped breathing out of nowhere, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did not mention the shake. I was frightened and not thinking, and I know that looks like hiding it.\""), .cross("You were yelling at the baby to stop crying before you picked the baby up, weren't you?", "\"I raised my voice because I was scared and frustrated. I had never done that before, and I regret it more than anything.\"")],
        openings: ("{D}, a nanny, was recorded on a nursery camera lifting a five-month-old baby and shaking for about seven seconds, after which the baby went limp. The hospital found bleeding under the skull and in both eyes, and the baby survived with seizures.", "The defense will present a choking emergency, a nanny trained a month earlier, and a physician who will explain how a rescue in panic can cause these injuries. A rescue gone wrong is not an intent to harm."),
        closings: ("A camera that recorded a seven-second shake, a baby who went limp, bleeding under the skull and behind both eyes, and a nanny who yelled to stop crying first. The video and the injuries match.", "The gagging on the audio, a history of reflux, and a nanny who panicked with a month-old training. The State has not proved that {D} meant to hurt the baby."),
        timeline: [(-30, "{DL} completes infant first-aid training."), (0, "Morning: the parents leave for work."), (0, "10:12 a.m.: the shake."), (0, "10:15 a.m.: {DL} calls 911.")],
        identified: "A nanny camera.",
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "expertTestimony"])

    static let exPostingCampaignV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.exPostingCampaign",
        category: .cyber,
        headlines: ["Woman Gets Dozens of Anonymous Texts Describing Her Daily Routine", "Texting App Account Traced to Ex's Email"],
        law: "cyberstalking",
        threshold: 5,
        spec: "Willfully harassed {V} by electronic communications, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 20...50,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After {V} ended the relationship, {V} began receiving anonymous texts through a free texting app. By {DATE}, 48 messages described {V}'s commute, gym times, and clothing, and one was emailed to {V}'s landlord. {V} blocked the app numbers four times. The app account was registered to an email address that {D} had used. {DL} says the details were common knowledge and a friend had {D.his} login.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Texting App Records", "48 messages from changing numbers, all tied to one account registered to {D}'s email."), E(.digital, 2, "Landlord Email", "An email to {V}'s landlord complaining about {V}'s \"guests.\"")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Friend Had Login", "{DL} says a friend had access to the account.")],
        role: "Victim",
        exam: [.direct("Tell us about your relationship with {D}.", "\"We were together for some time. I ended the relationship because I felt unsafe and unhappy, and I told {D} that I wanted no further contact.\""), .direct("What did you begin receiving after you ended the relationship?", "\"Anonymous texts through a free texting app. They came from changing numbers, and each one showed that someone knew where I was.\""), .direct("What did the messages say?", "\"They described when I left the house, what I wore, my commute, and my gym times. By {DATE}, there were 48 of them.\""), .direct("How did you try to stop them?", "\"I blocked the app numbers four times. Each time, a new number appeared, and the messages kept coming with more details.\""), .direct("What happened with your landlord?", "\"One of the messages was emailed to my landlord complaining about my guests. I had to explain to my landlord that I was being harassed.\""), .direct("How did you feel while this was happening?", "\"Afraid. I changed my routes, looked over my shoulder, and I did not feel safe at home or at the gym.\""), .cross("Did you see who sent the messages?", "\"No. I only saw the account records. The records tie the messages to an account registered to {DL}'s email, but I did not see who typed them.\""), .cross("Who knew your routine?", "\"A few people. {D.He} knew it best. But my friends, my gym, and my neighbors also knew parts of it.\""), .cross("Did a friend of the defendant have access to the account?", "\"{DL} says a friend did. I do not know that friend, and I cannot say what the friend did.\""), .cross("Did the defendant use the phrase scenic route?", "\"Yes. {DL} repeated that phrase from the messages in a text to a friend. I did not see that text myself.\""), .cross("Did the defendant ever contact you directly?", "\"Not that I know of. I did not hear from {DL} in person, and all the contact was by texts and the email.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} watched {V} and sent the details by text.", "A shared login and common knowledge."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry for what {V} went through.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} repeated a phrase from the messages, \"scenic route,\" in a text to a friend.", "The friend admitted using the account."),
        defendant: [.direct("Please describe your relationship with {V}.", "\"We were together for a while, and I cared about {V}. When it ended, I was hurt, but I accepted it and did not try to contact {V}.\""), .direct("Did you send the texts?", "\"No. I never sent them. I did not know about the messages until deputies came to talk to me.\""), .direct("Who had access to the account?", "\"A friend had my login. I made that account years ago and shared it with a friend, and the friend admitted using it.\""), .direct("Why was the account registered under your email?", "\"I made it years ago and never changed it. Several people used it, and I did not think about who was logging in.\""), .direct("What about the phrase scenic route?", "\"I say it a lot. It is a common phrase among my friends, and I used it in a text without thinking.\""), .direct("How are you coping with what happened?", "\"Right now I feel hurt and angry. I did not do this, and I am sorry that {V} was scared. I hope the real sender is found.\""), .cross("The account is registered to your email, isn't it?", "\"Yes. I made it years ago. I know that looks bad, but a friend also used it.\""), .cross("You knew {V}'s routine, didn't you?", "\"I knew some of it from when we were together. I know the commute and the gym, but I did not send anything.\""), .cross("You used the phrase scenic route in a text to a friend, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I say it often. I did not know it was in the messages until later.\""), .cross("The friend who used the account admitted it, didn't the friend?", "\"Yes. The friend admitted using the account. I did not know about it, and I did not ask the friend to do it.\""), .cross("You did not report the friend to deputies, did you?", "\"Not at first. I did not realize it mattered. I told them when they asked, and I gave them the friend's name.\"")],
        openings: ("After {V} ended the relationship, {V} began receiving anonymous texts through a free texting app. By {DATE}, 48 messages described {V}'s commute, gym times, and clothing, and the account was registered to an email that {D} used.", "The defense will present a shared login, a friend who admitted using the account, and a common phrase. Details that many people knew are not proof of who typed them."),
        closings: ("Forty-eight messages that tracked {V}'s day, an account registered to {D}'s email, and the phrase scenic route repeated by {D} in a text. The account and the phrase point to {D}.", "A shared login, a friend who admitted using the account, and a phrase that many people say. Anyone could have used it, and the State has not proved that {D} sent a single message."),
        timeline: [(-35, "{V} ends the relationship."), (-28, "The first anonymous text."), (-3, "The landlord email."), (0, "{V} reports to deputies.")],
        identified: "Texting app records.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        genders: ["D": .male, "V": .female])

    static let cityStranglerV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.cityStrangler",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Young Woman Strangled in Her Apartment; Delivery Driver Charged", "Confession Comes After Nine Hours, Lawyer Says"],
        law: "murder1",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "With premeditation and deliberation, killed {V} by strangulation in her apartment.",
        ages: 28...32,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V}, a young woman, was found strangled with a phone charger cord in her apartment on {DATE}. The door was not forced. {D}, a pizza delivery driver, had delivered to {V} twice that month. A ring doorbell showed a man in a delivery jacket knocking at 9:14 p.m. the night before. After nine hours of questioning, {DL} confessed. {DL} says the confession was false and the night was only a delivery.",
        state: [E(.statement, 3, "Confession", "{DL}'s recorded confession, giving the cord and the apartment layout."), E(.video, 3, "Doorbell Video", "A man in a delivery jacket knocks at 9:14 p.m.; the door opens and he goes inside."), E(.forensic, 2, "DNA Under Nails", "Male DNA under {V}'s nails, consistent with {DL}; the sample is partial.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Nine Hours", "The confession came after nine hours of questioning with no break for sleep."), E(.document, 2, "Delivery Log", "{DL}'s delivery log shows a call to {V}'s door at 9:10 p.m. and a drop at 9:20."), E(.forensic, 1, "Partial DNA", "The profile matches about one in 3,000 men.")],
        role: "Lead homicide detective",
        exam: [.direct("What are your duties as a homicide detective?", "\"I lead homicide investigations for the sheriff's office. I process scenes, review video, and conduct interviews, and I have worked many cases that began with a death in someone's home.\""), .direct("What did you find at {V}'s apartment on {DATE}?", "\"{V} was found strangled with a phone charger cord. The door was not forced, which told me {V} may have let the person in.\""), .direct("What did the doorbell video show?", "\"A person in a delivery jacket knocked at 9:14 the night before, the door opened, and the person went inside. The face is not clear on the video.\""), .direct("How did {D} come to your attention?", "\"{D} was a pizza delivery driver who had delivered to {V} twice that month. The delivery log shows a call to the door at 9:10 and a drop at 9:20.\""), .direct("What did the defendant say in the recorded confession?", "\"{D.He} described the cord and the layout of the apartment. I noted those details in the interview, and the confession was recorded.\""), .direct("What did the DNA under {V}'s nails show?", "\"A partial profile consistent with {DL}. It matches about one in 3,000 people, so it is not unique, but it fits.\""), .cross("How long was the interview?", "\"Nine hours. There was no break for sleep. I understand that is a long time, and I considered that when I reviewed it.\""), .cross("Did the details in the confession match what only the killer knew?", "\"Some did. {D.He} described the cord and the layout. But the layout could have been known from delivering there twice.\""), .cross("Was another person seen at the building that night?", "\"Yes. {V}'s former partner, who has a record of violence, was seen at the building that night. I looked into that, but the evidence pointed to {DL}.\""), .cross("Did the defendant keep anything of {V}'s?", "\"{V}'s phone charger was found in {DL}'s glove compartment. I cannot say how it got there or when.\""), .cross("Did the defendant recant?", "\"Yes. {D.He} said the confession was false and that it was only a delivery. {D.He} said so soon after the interview ended.\"")],
        defenseRole: "False confession expert",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Please describe your work on false confessions.", "\"I study how and why people confess to things they did not do. I review interview recordings and testify about the pressures that produce false confessions.\""), .direct("What factors make false confessions more likely?", "\"Long questioning, lack of sleep, isolation, and detectives who say they have proof. Together they can wear a person down until a confession seems like a way out.\""), .direct("What did you notice about this interview?", "\"Nine hours with no break for sleep. {D} began by denying it and later gave a statement that included details the detectives had supplied.\""), .direct("How can you tell whether details came from the person or from the detectives?", "\"By listening to who introduces each detail first. In this interview, the cord was mentioned by the detectives before {D.he} repeated it.\""), .direct("Are false confessions common?", "\"Not common, but they happen. In many documented wrongful convictions, a false confession was part of the case. It can be very persuasive to a jury.\""), .direct("What would you expect from a true confession?", "\"New facts that only the killer would know, and that police could then verify. I did not find any here.\""), .cross("Did you interview {D}?", "\"No. I reviewed the recording and the transcript. I cannot say what was in {D.his} mind during the interview.\""), .cross("Can you say that the defendant's confession was false?", "\"No. I cannot say that. I can say that the conditions raised the risk, and that I found some signs of contamination.\""), .cross("Did the defendant know the layout of the apartment from before?", "\"Yes. {D.He} had delivered to the apartment twice. That means the layout does not prove involvement in the killing.\""), .cross("Did the DNA match the defendant?", "\"A partial profile is consistent with {D.him}. I am not a DNA expert, and I did not review the laboratory work.\""), .cross("Is it possible a person confesses because they are guilty?", "\"Of course. Most confessions are true. I only discuss the risk factors in this one, and I leave the decision to the jury.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} entered {V}'s home and strangled {V.him}.", "A delivery, a tired suspect, and a false confession."),
        allocution: "\"I did not hurt {V}. I'm so sorry for the family.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} kept {V}'s phone charger in {D.his} glove compartment.", "{V}'s former boyfriend, who has a violence record, was seen at the building that night."),
        defendant: [.direct("What can you tell us about your job as a delivery driver?", "\"I deliver pizzas at night. I knock, hand over the order, and go. I deliver to dozens of apartments in a shift, and I do not remember most of them.\""), .direct("What happened at {V}'s door that night?", "\"I knocked, and {V} opened the door. I went in only to hand over the order and set the tray on a table, and then I left.\""), .direct("Why does your DNA appear under {V}'s nails?", "\"I touched the door and the tray. I do not know how it got under anyone's nails, and I did not hurt {V}.\""), .direct("Why did you confess?", "\"I had been questioned for nine hours without sleep. I wanted to go home, and I said what the detectives seemed to want.\""), .direct("How did you know about the cord and the apartment layout?", "\"I had delivered there twice, so I knew the layout. The detectives told me about the cord during the interview, and I repeated it.\""), .direct("What did you do after you left?", "\"I went to my next delivery. I finished my shift, and I did not hear about {V} until detectives came to find me.\""), .cross("You confessed on a recording, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I was exhausted and scared, and I said it was true. It was not.\""), .cross("You kept {V}'s phone charger in your glove compartment, didn't you?", "\"I found a charger in my car and did not know whose it was. I do not know how it got there.\""), .cross("You delivered to {V} twice that month, didn't you?", "\"Yes. That is why I knew the door and the layout. It does not mean I did anything.\""), .cross("The doorbell video shows a person in a delivery jacket going inside, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. That was me, delivering. I went in only for a moment, and I left.\""), .cross("You were alone with {V} that night, weren't you?", "\"For a minute or two, while I set the tray down. I know how that sounds, but I did nothing.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} was found strangled with a phone charger cord in an apartment where the door was not forced. {D}, a pizza delivery driver who had delivered there twice that month, was caught on a doorbell video, and after nine hours of questioning {D} confessed.", "The defense will present a tired delivery driver who said what detectives wanted after nine hours, an expert on false confessions, and another person with a record of violence seen at the building that night."),
        closings: ("A doorbell video of a delivery jacket entering at 9:14, a delivery log that ends at 9:20, DNA under {V}'s nails, and a recorded confession that described the cord and the apartment. The evidence points to {D}.", "Nine hours of questioning, details supplied by detectives, a partial DNA match that fits thousands of people, and another person with a violent record at the building. The State has not proved {D} did this."),
        timeline: [(-1, "9:14 p.m.: the doorbell video."), (-1, "9:20 p.m.: the delivery log ends."), (0, "{V} is found."), (3, "{DL} is questioned for nine hours.")],
        identified: "A doorbell video and a delivery log.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "voluntariness"],
        genders: ["D": .male, "V": .female])

    static let tipJarV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.tipJar",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Man Grabs Tip Jar at Farmers Market and Sprints Off", "Vendor's Phone Video Leads to Arrest"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        threshold: 5,
        spec: "Stole $73 in cash from a tip jar belonging to {V}, a market vendor, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...50,
        victim: true,
        summary: "On {DATE}, a man grabbed the tip jar from a farmers market stand while {V}, the vendor, was bagging produce, and ran. {V} filmed the back of a gray cap with a phone. A market volunteer chased the man and pointed him out to a deputy near the parking lot. {D} was holding $48 in small bills. {DL} says {D.he} found the jar abandoned.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Vendor's Phone", "A man in a gray cap grabs the jar at 9:05 a.m. and runs toward the lot."), E(.physical, 2, "Cash", "$48 in small bills in {D}'s hand; the jar was in a bush.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Found Jar", "{DL} says the jar was lying on the pavement.")],
        role: "Market vendor",
        exam: [.direct("Tell us about your stand at the farmers market.", "\"I sell produce at a stand every Saturday. I bag vegetables for customers, keep a tip jar on the corner of the table, and I know many regulars by name.\""), .direct("What happened at about 9:05 that morning?", "\"While I was bagging produce, a person in a gray cap grabbed the tip jar from the table and ran toward the parking lot.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I pulled out my phone and filmed the back of the gray cap as the person ran. I also shouted for help.\""), .direct("What happened after you shouted?", "\"A market volunteer chased the person and pointed out {D} to a deputy near the parking lot a few minutes later.\""), .direct("How much was in the jar?", "\"About $73 in small bills, mostly ones and fives. It was the tips from the first part of the morning and from the week before.\""), .direct("What was found when {D} was stopped?", "\"{D.He} was holding $48 in small bills. The jar itself was found in a bush near the lot.\""), .cross("Did you see the face of the person who took the jar?", "\"Not clearly. I saw the back of a gray cap and part of a jacket. I cannot say for sure who it was.\""), .cross("Was the jar on the table or on the corner?", "\"On the corner of the table. A person walking by could reach it without stepping up to the stand.\""), .cross("Did you see the defendant take it?", "\"No. I saw the person in the gray cap, and the volunteer later pointed {DL} out. I did not identify {DL} myself.\""), .cross("Was the cap on the video identical to the one the defendant wore?", "\"It looks very similar. Many people wear that kind of cap, so I cannot say for certain.\""), .cross("Did the amount in the defendant's hand match what was missing?", "\"It was $48, and I had about $73 in the jar. It was less, and I cannot say what happened to the rest.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} grabbed a tip jar and ran.", "An abandoned jar found on the ground."),
        allocution: "\"I took it. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} was wearing a gray cap identical to the one on the video.", "{DL} was walking toward the stand when someone else dropped the jar and ran."),
        defendant: [.direct("Walk us through what you were doing at the market that morning.", "\"I was walking through the market to buy vegetables. I wore a gray cap, as I do most days, and I was heading toward a stand near the lot.\""), .direct("How did you come to have the cash in your hand?", "\"I found the jar lying on the pavement and picked it up. I took out the money to count it so I could return it.\""), .direct("Why did you leave the jar in a bush?", "\"I did not want to carry an empty jar. I put it down and was heading to the stand to hand over the cash when the volunteer stopped me.\""), .direct("Did you take the jar from the stand?", "\"No. I did not. Someone else dropped it and ran, and I was walking toward the stand when I saw it on the ground.\""), .direct("What did you do when the volunteer and the deputy stopped you?", "\"I told them I found it and was going to hand it over. I gave the deputy the money and explained what happened.\""), .direct("How do you feel about being accused?", "\"Embarrassed, more than anything. I tried to do the right thing, and I ended up in court. I should have handed the jar over right away.\""), .cross("You were wearing a gray cap identical to the one on the video, weren't you?", "\"Yes. It is a common style, and I wear it often. I know it looks bad, but plenty of people wear one.\""), .cross("You had $48 in your hand, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I took it out of the jar to count it. I was going to hand it over, but I did not reach the stand.\""), .cross("You put the jar in a bush, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did not want to carry it. I know now that was a mistake, and I should have kept it in my hand.\""), .cross("Someone ran toward the lot with the jar, didn't they?", "\"I did not see who ran. I saw someone drop the jar and run, and I picked it up from the pavement.\""), .cross("You never told the vendor you had found the jar until the deputy stopped you, did you?", "\"No. I did not get the chance. I was on my way to do it when the volunteer stopped me.\"")],
        openings: ("On {DATE}, a person in a gray cap grabbed the tip jar from a farmers market stand while {V}, the vendor, was bagging produce, and ran. {V} filmed the back of the cap, a volunteer chased the person, and {D} was found holding $48 in small bills.", "The defense will explain that {D} found the jar lying on the pavement after someone else dropped it and ran, and was on the way to return it. Holding found money is not a theft."),
        closings: ("A person in a gray cap grabbing the jar on a vendor's video, a volunteer who chased the person, and $48 in small bills in {D}'s hand with the jar in a bush. The cap and the cash fit.", "A jar lying on the pavement, a common cap, and a person who was walking toward the stand to hand it over. No one saw the face of the person who ran, and the State has not proved it was {D}."),
        timeline: [(0, "9 a.m.: the market opens."), (0, "9:05 a.m.: the jar is taken."), (0, "9:10 a.m.: the volunteer points out {DL}."), (0, "9:20 a.m.: the arrest.")],
        identified: "A vendor's phone video and a volunteer.",
        mood: .indifferent,
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let churchTreasurerSkimV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.churchTreasurerSkim",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Building Fund Checks Deposited in Second Bank Account, Church Says", "Audit Finds Pledge Checks Endorsed at Wrong Bank"],
        law: "embezzlement",
        threshold: 6,
        spec: "Embezzled $6,800 entrusted to {D} by {V}, a church, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 35...70,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A church's building fund received pledge checks all year, but the main account showed only part of them. An auditor found 19 checks totaling $6,800 endorsed and deposited at another bank into an account in the church's name that only {D}, the treasurer, controlled. The account was drained by {DATE}. {DL} says it was a separate holding account for a grant.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Second Account Statements", "19 checks totaling $6,800 deposited into an account only {D} controlled."), E(.document, 3, "Withdrawals", "Cash withdrawals and a payment to {D}'s card on the account."), E(.document, 1, "Pledge Ledger", "The ledger lists the 19 pledges as paid.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Grant Holding", "{DL} says the account was set up for a grant."), E(.document, 1, "Receipts", "Receipts for church supplies bought with some of the funds.")],
        role: "Church auditor",
        exam: [.direct("Tell us about your work as a church auditor.", "\"I audit the books of congregations. I compare bank statements, ledgers, and deposit records to make sure offerings and pledges are properly counted and spent.\""), .direct("What did you notice about the building fund?", "\"Pledge checks came in all year, but the main account showed only part of them. The totals did not match the pledge ledger.\""), .direct("What did you find at the other bank?", "\"19 checks totaling $6,800 had been endorsed and deposited into a second account in the church's name. Only {D}, the treasurer, controlled it.\""), .direct("What did the second account statements show?", "\"The deposits, followed by cash withdrawals and payments to a credit card. The account was drained by the date of the audit.\""), .direct("What did the pledge ledger show?", "\"It listed the same 19 pledges as paid. The church believed the money had arrived, but it never reached the main account.\""), .direct("What happened when the board confronted {D}?", "\"{D.He} said it was a separate holding account for a grant. I asked for grant documents, and I did not receive any.\""), .cross("Was the second account opened in the church's name?", "\"Yes. It was opened in the church's name, at a bank that the grant sponsor required. That part matches what {D.he} said.\""), .cross("Were some purchases made for the church from that account?", "\"A few. There are receipts for church supplies bought with some of the funds. I did not dispute those.\""), .cross("Did the board know about the account?", "\"Some members may have known. There was no formal vote to approve a second account, and I cannot say who was told.\""), .cross("Did you find a grant?", "\"No. I did not find any grant payment or award letter. {D.He} said it was pending, but nothing ever arrived.\""), .cross("Was there a personal payment from the account?", "\"Yes. A credit card in {D.his} name was paid from the account. {D.He} says it was a reimbursement, and I did not see documents for that.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Church deacon",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Describe your role as a deacon for the jury.", "\"I serve on the board of deacons. We oversee the church's finances and ministries, and we meet monthly to hear reports from the treasurer.\""), .direct("What did {D} tell the board about a grant?", "\"{D} said there might be a grant for the building fund and that a separate account would be needed. We listened, but we did not take a formal vote.\""), .direct("Did the board formally approve a second account?", "\"Not formally. I remember a conversation about it, but no motion and no vote. We were informal, and that was our mistake.\""), .direct("What kind of treasurer was the defendant?", "\"Dedicated and organized, with long hours. {DF} kept the books and gave reports, and we trusted {DF} without checking the bank statements.\""), .direct("What did you think when the auditor found the account?", "\"I was shocked. I did not know pledge checks were going there. I knew about a grant account, but not that it held pledges.\""), .direct("What could the board have done differently?", "\"We should have required two signers and reviewed the statements. We did not do either, and I think that is a failure of the board.\""), .cross("Did the defendant ask for permission before using pledge checks?", "\"I do not recall. I did not hear that request, and I do not think the board knew the checks were being deposited there.\""), .cross("Did you see any grant documents?", "\"No. I never saw a letter or an award. I only heard that one was expected, and I did not ask for proof.\""), .cross("Did you know the defendant paid a personal credit card from the account?", "\"No. I did not know that until the audit. That would have been a problem if it was not approved.\""), .cross("Would you have approved the card payment?", "\"Not without receipts. I would have wanted to see documents, and I would have asked the board to vote.\""), .cross("The board never voted to open a second account, did it?", "\"No. The board never voted on it. I understood the grant paperwork required it, and I did not check that claim.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} routed pledge checks to a private account.", "A holding account for a grant."),
        allocution: "\"I should have told the board. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} paid a personal credit card from the account.", "The account was opened at a bank the grant sponsor required."),
        defendant: [.direct("Describe your time as church treasurer for the jury.", "\"I volunteered as treasurer for several years. I paid bills, kept records, and tried to find money for the building fund.\""), .direct("Why did you open a second account?", "\"For a grant. The sponsor required a particular bank, and I was told to hold funds there. I thought I was helping the church.\""), .direct("Why did you deposit pledge checks into that account?", "\"I thought they could count toward the grant match. I should have asked the board first, and I did not understand how it would look.\""), .direct("Did the board know about the account?", "\"Some of them did. I mentioned it in a meeting, but I never got a formal vote, and I know that was a mistake.\""), .direct("What about the credit card payment?", "\"It was a reimbursement for church expenses I paid myself. I did not keep all the receipts, and I know that looks bad.\""), .direct("What happened to the grant?", "\"It never came. The sponsor delayed, and then I was confronted before the grant was approved. I wish I had told the board sooner.\""), .cross("You paid your own credit card from the account, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I thought it was a fair reimbursement, but I know I should have asked first.\""), .cross("The account was drained by the time of the audit, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. It was. Some went to church supplies and some to other things, and I did not track every dollar.\""), .cross("Only you controlled the account, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I was the only signer. I should have added another signer, and I did not.\""), .cross("You did not tell the board the checks went to the second account, did you?", "\"Not in detail. I mentioned a grant account, but I did not tell them that pledge checks were being deposited there.\""), .cross("No grant ever arrived, did it?", "\"No. It did not. I understand why the board felt misled, and I am sorry for it.\"")],
        openings: ("A church's building fund received pledge checks all year, but the main account showed only part of them. An auditor found 19 checks totaling $6,800 deposited into a second account that only {D}, the treasurer, controlled, and the account was drained.", "The defense will present an account opened at a bank the grant sponsor required, a board that knew of a grant account, and a treasurer with good intentions. A poorly run account is not a theft."),
        closings: ("Nineteen pledge checks totaling $6,800 in a second account that only {D} controlled, cash withdrawals, and a payment to {D}'s own credit card. The ledger says the pledges were paid, and the church never got the money.", "A holding account for a grant at a bank the sponsor required, church supplies bought from it, and no formal rules at the church. The State has not proved that {D} meant to steal."),
        timeline: [(-300, "The pledge drive starts."), (-120, "The second account opens."), (-10, "The auditor compares totals."), (0, "The board confronts {DL}.")],
        identified: "An audit of pledge checks.",
        aggravating: ["The defendant took advantage of a position of trust or confidence"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "The congregation gave what it could.")

    static let erScuffleV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.erScuffle",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Driver Blocks Ambulance Bay, Pulls Away From Deputy", "Body Camera Shows Dispute Over Parked Car at Hospital"],
        law: "resisting",
        threshold: 5,
        spec: "Resisted, delayed, and obstructed a public officer in discharging a duty of {D.his} office, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 20...60,
        victim: false,
        summary: "A deputy found {D}'s car parked in a hospital ambulance bay on {DATE} while an ambulance waited. The deputy told {D} to move it twice. {D} refused, then yanked {D.his} arm away when the deputy reached to guide {D.him} toward the car. {DL} says {D.he} had rushed a relative in and could not find parking.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Body Camera", "{D} refuses twice, then pulls away from the deputy's hand."), E(.statement, 2, "Ambulance Crew", "The crew says they were delayed about three minutes.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Relative Inside", "{DL} says a relative was being admitted and {D.he} was frantic.")],
        role: "Sheriff's deputy",
        exam: [.direct("What does your work as a deputy involve?", "\"I patrol the county and respond to calls at hospitals, businesses, and homes. I wear a body camera, and I give orders to move vehicles that block emergency access.\""), .direct("What did you find at the hospital on {DATE}?", "\"{D}'s car was parked in the ambulance bay while an ambulance waited to unload. The bay is marked and reserved for emergency vehicles.\""), .direct("What did you tell {D}?", "\"I told {D.him} twice to move the car. I explained that an ambulance was waiting and the car had to go right away.\""), .direct("How did the defendant respond?", "\"{D.He} refused both times and said, I'm not moving it. {D.He} also yelled at the ambulance crew.\""), .direct("What happened when you reached to guide the defendant?", "\"I put a hand on {DL}'s arm to guide {DL} toward the car. {DL} yanked the arm away, and I told {DL} that was resisting.\""), .direct("How long was the ambulance delayed?", "\"The crew says they were delayed about three minutes. That can matter a great deal when a patient is in the ambulance.\""), .cross("Did the defendant strike you?", "\"No. {D.He} pulled the arm away, but did not hit me or push me. I was not hurt.\""), .cross("Was a relative inside the hospital?", "\"Yes. {D.He} said a relative was being admitted, and {D.he} was frantic. I later confirmed that with the hospital.\""), .cross("Did the defendant hear the first order?", "\"I am not sure. A nurse had called {DL}'s phone about then, and {DL} may have been on the call when I gave the first order.\""), .cross("Was {D} calm when you spoke?", "\"No. {D.He} was shaking and upset. I could see that {D.he} was afraid, and I understood that.\""), .cross("Did the defendant move the car afterward?", "\"Yes. {D.He} moved it after I made the second order and after the incident, and {D.he} apologized.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} ignored an order and pulled away from a deputy.", "A frantic family member."),
        allocution: "\"I was scared. I'm sorry.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} yelled, \"I'm not moving it,\" at the crew.", "{DL} had no time to hear the first order because of a call from a nurse."),
        defendant: [.direct("Tell us why you were at the hospital.", "\"I rushed a relative in who was very sick. I was scared and I was not thinking about anything else but getting help quickly.\""), .direct("Why did you park in the ambulance bay?", "\"I could not find a space. It was the nearest spot to the door, and I thought I would only be there for a moment.\""), .direct("Did you hear the deputy's first order?", "\"Not the first one. A nurse called my phone and I was on the call. I did not realize the deputy was talking to me.\""), .direct("What did you say to the ambulance crew?", "\"I yelled, I'm not moving it. I was panicking and I wanted to go inside. I should have listened and moved the car.\""), .direct("Why did you pull your arm away?", "\"I was shaking and I did not understand what was happening. I thought the deputy was grabbing me, and I reacted without thinking.\""), .direct("How has this affected you?", "\"I would say I feel ashamed. I should have moved the car right away. I delayed an ambulance, and I am sorry to the crew.\""), .cross("You were told twice to move the car, weren't you?", "\"Yes. I was told twice. I heard the second order, and I did not move right away.\""), .cross("You refused the second order, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I said I would not move it. I was frightened for my relative, and I know that does not excuse it.\""), .cross("You pulled your arm from the deputy's hand, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I jerked away. I was shaking, and I did not mean to resist, but I did pull away.\""), .cross("The ambulance was delayed because of your car, wasn't it?", "\"About three minutes, they say. I did not know the ambulance was waiting, and I should have asked.\""), .cross("You moved the car only after the incident, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I moved it after the deputy ordered me again and after I pulled away. I apologized to the crew.\"")],
        openings: ("A deputy found {D}'s car parked in a hospital ambulance bay on {DATE} while an ambulance waited. The deputy told {D} to move it twice, {D} refused, and then {D} yanked an arm away when the deputy reached to guide {D} toward the car.", "The defense will present a frightened family member who had just rushed a relative in, a nurse's call that covered the first order, and an apology afterward. Panic is not a plan to resist."),
        closings: ("A car in an ambulance bay, two orders to move it, a refusal on camera, and a pull away from the deputy's hand. The ambulance crew was delayed about three minutes, and the camera shows it all.", "A frightened family member who could not find a space, a phone call that covered the first order, and an arm pulled back in fear. The State has not proved that {D} meant to resist."),
        timeline: [(0, "Evening: {DL} drives a relative in."), (0, "7:10 p.m.: the car in the bay."), (0, "7:14 p.m.: the deputy's second order."), (0, "7:16 p.m.: {DL} pulls away.")],
        identified: "A body camera.",
        mood: .sympathetic)

    static let pruittMillRoadV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.pruittMillRoad",
        category: .traffic,
        headlines: ["Cyclist Left in Ditch at Dawn; White Work Van Sought", "Hit-and-Run Case Rests on a Partial Tag and Paint Transfer"],
        law: "hitAndRun",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Being the driver of a vehicle involved in a crash on a county road that caused serious bodily injury to {V}, and knowing or having reason to know of the crash, willfully failed to stop and remain at the scene.",
        ages: 30...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "At about 5:50 a.m. on {DATE}, {V} was riding a bicycle to work along the edge of a county road when a white work van struck {V.him} from behind and kept going. A jogger found {V} in the ditch ten minutes later with a broken leg and collarbone. A driver following behind caught the first three characters of the tag. White paint on {V}'s bike matched a van repainted two years earlier. A week later, {D}'s van had a new headlight and a dented panel. {DL} says the dent came from a loading dock and the van was lent out that morning.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Paint Transfer", "White paint on the bike frame matches the repainted finish on {DL}'s van."), E(.statement, 2, "Partial Tag", "A following driver saw the first three characters, which match {DL}'s tag."), E(.document, 2, "Repair Receipt", "{DL} paid cash for a new headlight and panel work four days after the crash."), E(.video, 1, "Gas Station Camera", "A white van passes the gas station toward the road at 5:46 a.m.; the tag is out of frame.")],
        defense: [E(.document, 3, "Fleet Records", "State records list 640 white work vans registered across three counties."), E(.statement, 2, "Lent Out", "{DL} says a coworker borrowed the van that morning to haul tile."), E(.forensic, 2, "No Trace on Van", "No blood, fibers, or hair were found on the van.")],
        role: "State trooper",
        exam: [.direct("What does your work as a state trooper involve?", "\"I investigate crashes on county and state roads. I collect physical evidence, interview witnesses, and trace vehicles from paint, parts, and registration records.\""), .direct("What happened on the morning of {DATE}?", "\"At about 5:50, {V} was riding a bicycle to work along the edge of a county road when a white work van struck {V} from behind and kept going.\""), .direct("How was {V} found?", "\"A jogger found {V} in the ditch about ten minutes later with a broken leg and a broken collarbone. {V} was taken to the hospital.\""), .direct("What did you recover from the bike?", "\"White paint on the frame that matches the repainted finish on {D}'s van. The van was repainted two years earlier, so the finish is distinctive.\""), .direct("What did the following driver see?", "\"The first three characters of the tag, which match {D.his} tag. The driver could not see the rest because of distance and the angle.\""), .direct("What did you learn about the repair?", "\"Four days after the crash, {D.he} paid cash for a new headlight and panel work. A week later, the van had a new headlight and a dented panel.\""), .cross("How many white work vans are registered in the area?", "\"State records list 640 white work vans across three counties. Many of them are common models, and the paint may not be unique.\""), .cross("Was blood or fiber found on {D}'s van?", "\"No. No blood, fibers, or hair were found on the van. It was repaired and cleaned before we examined it.\""), .cross("Did the gas station camera show the tag?", "\"It shows a white van passing at 5:46 heading toward the road, but the tag was out of frame.\""), .cross("Did the defendant say anyone else drove the van?", "\"Yes. {D.He} said a coworker borrowed the van that morning to haul tile. I have not been able to identify the coworker.\""), .cross("Where was the defendant's phone at 5:50?", "\"About fifty miles away, at a job site. That fits what {D.he} told me, and I cannot explain it away.\"")],
        defenseRole: "{DL}'s coworker",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Explain to the jury how you know {D}.", "\"I work with {D} on tile jobs. We share equipment, and we often share the van. I have known {DF} for several years.\""), .direct("Did anyone else drive the van?", "\"Sometimes. We lend each other equipment and vehicles. I know of several people who have driven it, though not on that morning.\""), .direct("What do you know about the dent?", "\"{DF} told me it happened at a loading dock. I saw the dent later and the new headlight, and {DF} did not hide it from anyone.\""), .direct("What did the defendant say about the morning of the crash?", "\"{DF} said {DF} was at a job site fifty miles away and that someone borrowed the van. {DF} seemed shocked when deputies came.\""), .direct("What is the defendant like at work?", "\"Careful and honest. {DF} follows safety rules and takes pride in the work. I cannot imagine {DF} leaving someone in a ditch.\""), .direct("Do other people use white vans like the defendant's?", "\"Yes. Many contractors do. I see white work vans all over the county, and some look almost identical.\""), .cross("Did you borrow the van that morning?", "\"Not that morning. I did borrow it other times. I do not know who borrowed it that morning.\""), .cross("Who borrowed it?", "\"I do not know. {DF} said someone did, but I did not see who. I did not ask {DF} for a name.\""), .cross("Where were you at 5:50 that morning?", "\"At home, asleep. I cannot say who had the van, and I only know what {D.he} told me.\""), .cross("Did the defendant tell you about the crash?", "\"Not until later. {D.He} said deputies came and asked about the van. I was surprised, and I told {D.him} to get a lawyer.\""), .cross("Did {D} pay cash for the repair?", "\"I heard so. I do not know why. I thought it was just a way to save money, but I cannot say.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} hit a cyclist and drove off.", "A common van and a borrowed ride."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry for what {V} went through.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} texted a friend, \"Hit something on the road. Not sure what.\" that morning.", "{DL}'s phone shows {D.him} fifty miles away at a job site at 5:50 a.m."),
        defendant: [.direct("Tell us about your work.", "\"I do tile and flooring jobs, and I use a white work van to haul materials. I drive it every day, and I have owned it for several years.\""), .direct("Were you driving the van that morning?", "\"No. I was at a job site fifty miles away at 5:50. A coworker borrowed the van that morning to haul tile.\""), .direct("How did the van get dented?", "\"At a loading dock. I backed into a post, and the dent and headlight were damaged. I fixed it a few days later.\""), .direct("Why did you pay cash for the repair?", "\"It was cheaper. The shop gave a discount for cash. I did not think about how it would look afterward.\""), .direct("What did you text a friend that morning?", "\"I wrote, Hit something on the road. Not sure what. I meant my coworker had told me the van hit something, and I did not know any details.\""), .direct("Looking back, how do you feel about what happened to {V}?", "\"I feel terrible. I did not know until deputies came. I hope {V} recovers, and I wish I could help.\""), .cross("The paint on the bike matches your van, doesn't it?", "\"It is a common repaint. I do not know what that match means. I did not hit {V}.\""), .cross("Your tag begins with the same three characters, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. Many tags share those characters. I was not driving, so I cannot say more.\""), .cross("You paid cash for repairs four days after the crash, didn't you?", "\"Yes. It looks bad. But the dent came from the loading dock, and I did not do anything wrong.\""), .cross("You cannot name the coworker who borrowed the van, can you?", "\"I know the coworker by a first name. I have not been able to reach that person since. I know that is a weakness.\""), .cross("You texted that you hit something on the road, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did write that. I was repeating what I was told, and I did not mean I was the one driving.\"")],
        openings: ("At about 5:50 on the morning of {DATE}, {V} was riding a bicycle along a county road when a white work van struck {V} from behind and kept going. White paint on the bike matches {D}'s van, a following driver saw the first three characters of the tag, and {D} paid cash for repairs.", "The defense will present a common white van among 640 registered in the area, a phone fifty miles away at the time of the crash, and a coworker who borrowed the van. No blood or fiber was found on it."),
        closings: ("White paint matching {D}'s repainted van, the first three characters of {D}'s tag, a cash repair four days after the crash, and a text that said hit something on the road. {V} was left in a ditch.", "A common van, a phone fifty miles away at 5:50, and no blood or fiber on the vehicle. The State has not proved that {D} was driving when {V} was struck."),
        timeline: [(0, "5:46 a.m.: a white van passes the gas station."), (0, "5:50 a.m.: {V} is struck."), (0, "6 a.m.: a jogger finds {V}."), (4, "{DL} pays for repairs.")],
        identified: "Paint transfer and a partial tag.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "eyewitnessID"])

    static let sharedApartmentV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.sharedApartment",
        category: .drugs,
        headlines: ["Cocaine Baggies Found Above Washer in Shared House", "Housemates Point Fingers After Raid"],
        law: "pwisd",
        threshold: 4,
        spec: "Possessed cocaine with intent to sell or deliver.",
        ages: 21...34,
        victim: false,
        summary: "On {DATE}, deputies executed a search warrant at a four-bedroom rental house leased to {D} and shared with three housemates. In a cabinet above the laundry room washer they found 18 baggies of cocaine totaling 14.9 grams, a scale, and $960. {DL} was the only one home. A housemate with a prior sale conviction left town two days later. {DL} says the laundry cabinet is shared and none of it was {D.his}.",
        state: [E(.physical, 3, "Laundry Cabinet", "Eighteen knotted baggies of white powder, a scale, and $960 in a cabinet above the washer.", .search), E(.forensic, 2, "Lab Report", "Cocaine, net weight 14.9 grams."), E(.digital, 2, "Phone Messages", "{DL}'s phone has texts such as 'Got 2? Same as last time.' sent in the past two weeks.", .search)],
        defense: [E(.document, 3, "Housemate Record", "A housemate has a prior conviction for selling cocaine and left town two days after the search."), E(.forensic, 2, "Prints", "Two usable prints on the cabinet; neither matches {DL}."), E(.document, 1, "Pay Stubs", "{DL} works full time at a hardware warehouse.")],
        role: "Narcotics detective",
        exam: [.direct("Tell us about your work as a narcotics detective.", "\"I investigate drug sales for the sheriff's office. I review phone evidence, work with informants, and help serve search warrants on homes where drugs are sold.\""), .direct("What did you find at the house on {DATE}?", "\"In a cabinet above the laundry room washer, we found 18 baggies of cocaine totaling 14.9 grams, a scale, and $960.\""), .direct("Who was home when you served the warrant?", "\"Only {D}. The house is a four-bedroom rental leased to {D.him} and shared with three housemates, and the others were not there.\""), .direct("What did the lab report show?", "\"The substance was cocaine with a net weight of 14.9 grams. The baggies and the scale are consistent with sales.\""), .direct("What did you find on {D}'s phone?", "\"Texts with a buyer that mentioned meeting up and prices. I took them as possible drug talk, and that was part of why I linked them to the cabinet.\""), .direct("What happened with one of the housemates?", "\"A housemate with a prior conviction for selling cocaine left town two days after the search. We have not been able to locate that housemate.\""), .cross("Whose prints were on the cabinet?", "\"Two usable prints were found. Neither matches {DL}. They have not been matched to anyone else yet.\""), .cross("Who else used the laundry room?", "\"All three housemates. The washer and the cabinet are shared, and people keep detergent and cleaning supplies there.\""), .cross("Did the defendant have a job?", "\"Yes. {D.He} works full time at a hardware warehouse. The pay stubs show regular wages.\""), .cross("What were the texts really about?", "\"{DL} says they were about a friend's used speakers. The buyer was someone {DL} met outside the house, and I have not disproved that.\""), .cross("Did you find drugs in the defendant's bedroom?", "\"No. Nothing was found in {D.his} room. All of it was in the shared cabinet above the washer.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Former housemate",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Walk us through how you know {D}.", "\"I was a housemate for a while. We shared the house and the laundry, and I knew {D} as a quiet person who worked a lot.\""), .direct("Who used the laundry cabinet?", "\"Everyone did, for detergent and cleaning products. It was above the washer, and anyone who did laundry could reach it.\""), .direct("Did the defendant ever sell drugs that you knew of?", "\"No. I never saw {DF} sell anything. {DF} worked at a warehouse and came home tired most nights.\""), .direct("What did you notice about the other housemates?", "\"One had a past with drugs and was often out late. I never saw anything in the cabinet, but I did not look.\""), .direct("What did you think when you heard about the search?", "\"I was shocked. I could not believe that drugs were in the cabinet. I told the deputies that {D.he} was not the type.\""), .direct("Why did you move out?", "\"I found another place after a few months. It had nothing to do with {DF}, and I still think of {DF} as a friend.\""), .cross("Did you see baggies in the cabinet?", "\"No. I never saw baggies. I only used the cabinet for detergent, and I did not look at the shelves above.\""), .cross("Did you see what the other housemates kept there?", "\"No. I did not check. I do not know what anyone else kept there.\""), .cross("Were you home during the search?", "\"No. I was gone by then. I heard about it afterward from another housemate.\""), .cross("Did you know the housemate with the conviction?", "\"Yes, a little. I did not know about the conviction at the time. I do not know why the person left.\""), .cross("Did the defendant ever meet people outside the house?", "\"Sometimes. {D.He} met friends and buyers for used items. I did not know what was said in those meetings.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} kept cocaine to sell above the washer.", "A shared cabinet and a housemate who ran."),
        allocution: "\"I should have known what was going on in my house.\"",
        truths: ("The texts on {DL}'s phone were with a buyer {DL} met outside the house.", "The texts were about a friend's used speakers, not drugs."),
        defendant: [.direct("Tell the jury about living in the shared house.", "\"I lease the house and share it with three housemates. We split the rent, and we share the laundry room, the kitchen, and the cabinets.\""), .direct("Do you know whose drugs were in the cabinet?", "\"No. They were not mine. I have never kept drugs in that cabinet, and I did not know anyone did.\""), .direct("What were the texts about?", "\"Used speakers. A friend had speakers to sell, and I met a buyer outside the house to look at them. Nothing to do with drugs.\""), .direct("What do you know about the housemate who left?", "\"A housemate with an old conviction left town two days after the search. The housemate said there was a job elsewhere.\""), .direct("What was the $960 in the cabinet?", "\"I do not know. It was not mine. My cash is in my room, and I pay the rent by check.\""), .direct("Looking back, how do you feel about being charged?", "\"Mostly I feel confused and angry. I work full time, I pay the rent, and I did not know about any drugs in the house.\""), .cross("You leased the house, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I signed the lease and I am responsible for it. I know that is why I am here.\""), .cross("You were the only one home during the search, weren't you?", "\"Yes. The others were out. I did not know the deputies were coming, and I did not hide anything.\""), .cross("The texts mention prices, don't they?", "\"They mention prices for speakers. I understand how a text about a price can be misread, but they were about speakers.\""), .cross("The prints on the cabinet are not yours, are they?", "\"No. They are not. I rarely use the cabinet, and I do not know whose prints they are.\""), .cross("The housemate who left had a conviction for selling cocaine, didn't the housemate?", "\"Yes. I did not know about it when we signed the lease. I found out after the search.\"")],
        openings: ("On {DATE}, deputies searched a four-bedroom rental house leased to {D} and found 18 baggies of cocaine totaling 14.9 grams, a scale, and $960 in a cabinet above the laundry room washer. {D} was the only one home, and the texts on {D}'s phone mentioned prices.", "The defense will present a shared cabinet, prints that do not match {D}, a housemate with a sale conviction who left town two days later, and texts about used speakers. Sharing a house is not sharing guilt."),
        closings: ("Eighteen baggies, a scale, and $960 in a cabinet in the house {D} leases, and texts that mention prices. {D} was the only one home when deputies arrived.", "A shared cabinet used by three housemates, prints that are not {D}'s, and a housemate with a sale conviction who left town two days later. The State has not proved the cocaine was {D}'s."),
        timeline: [(-14, "The texts begin."), (0, "Morning: the warrant is served."), (2, "A housemate leaves town."), (30, "The lab report arrives.")],
        identified: "A search warrant for the house.",
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "searchSeizure"])

    static let noteBanditV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.noteBandit",
        category: .robbery,
        headlines: ["Man in Safety Vest Passes Deposit-Slip Notes at Four Credit Unions", "Transit Card Records Lead to Suspect in Bank Note Robberies"],
        law: "commonLawRobbery",
        threshold: 10,
        spec: "Took $2,950 from a teller at a credit union branch by passing a note threatening violence.",
        ages: 48...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "Over six weeks, four credit union branches were robbed the same way: a man in an orange safety vest and a ballcap wrote a threat on a deposit slip and slid it to the teller, then took the cash and walked to a bus stop. On {DATE}, {V}, the fourth teller, handed over $2,950 and later found the slip with a fingerprint. A transit card tapped at the stop was linked to {D}. {DL} admits being near the last branch but denies the rest and says {D.he} was only there for a bus.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Branch Cameras", "Four videos of a man in an orange vest passing deposit slips; the last shows the slip."), E(.forensic, 3, "Fingerprint", "A print on the fourth slip matches {DL}."), E(.digital, 2, "Transit Card Records", "A card registered to {DL} was tapped at the stop after three robberies."), E(.physical, 2, "Vest and Cap", "An orange vest and ballcap found in a dumpster behind {DL}'s building.", .search)],
        defense: [E(.document, 3, "First Robbery Alibi", "A pharmacy receipt places {DL} across town 20 minutes before the first robbery."), E(.document, 2, "Public Slips", "Deposit slips are on a public counter, so many hands touch them."), E(.statement, 1, "No Weapon", "No weapon was shown or found.")],
        role: "Credit union teller",
        exam: [.direct("Tell us about your job at the credit union.", "\"I work as a teller at the credit union. I take deposits, cash checks, and count my drawer, and I try to stay calm when customers get upset.\""), .direct("What happened at your window on {DATE}?", "\"A person in an orange safety vest and a ballcap slid a deposit slip across the counter. A threat was written on it, and I felt my stomach drop.\""), .direct("What did the slip say?", "\"Give me the 20s. I have something. I did not know whether that meant a weapon, so I handed over the cash.\""), .direct("How much did you give?", "\"$2,950. I counted it into a stack and slid it across. The person took it and walked out toward the bus stop.\""), .direct("What did you do with the slip afterward?", "\"I saved it and handed it to deputies. I did not touch it more than I had to, and a fingerprint was found on it.\""), .direct("How did this affect you?", "\"I was shaken for days. I kept thinking about the note and wondering whether I should have done something differently.\""), .cross("Did you see a weapon?", "\"No. No weapon was shown, and none was found. The note said I have something, but I never saw anything.\""), .cross("Could you identify the face?", "\"Not for sure. The ballcap and vest were what I noticed. I could not say it was {D} based on the face.\""), .cross("Did the person hurt you or threaten you aloud?", "\"No. The person never spoke. The threat was only on the slip, and I was not touched.\""), .cross("Are deposit slips on a public counter?", "\"Yes. They sit on a public counter in the lobby. Many customers touch them every day.\""), .cross("Did you see which way the person went?", "\"Toward the bus stop outside. I watched through the window until the person was out of sight.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Pharmacy clerk",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Describe your job at the pharmacy for the jury.", "\"I work the counter at a pharmacy. I fill orders, ring up customers, and print receipts that show the date, time, and items purchased.\""), .direct("Do you remember {D} coming in on the morning of the first robbery?", "\"Yes. {D} bought a prescription around eleven. The receipt shows the time, and I remember because {D.he} paid in cash.\""), .direct("How reliable is the time on your receipts?", "\"Very. The register stamps the time automatically. It is checked against our system clock each day, and it has never been off by more than a minute.\""), .direct("How far is the pharmacy from the first credit union?", "\"About ten miles, across town. It would take at least twenty minutes by bus or car, depending on traffic.\""), .direct("What did the defendant seem like that morning?", "\"Tired and a little anxious, but calm. {D.He} did not seem rushed, and {D.he} took time to pick up the medication.\""), .direct("Did you speak to deputies?", "\"Yes. I gave them the receipt and the time. I told them what I remembered about {DF} at the counter.\""), .cross("Did you note the time yourself?", "\"The receipt did. I was not watching a clock, and I only know the time from the register.\""), .cross("Do you know where the defendant went after leaving?", "\"No. I did not see. I only know {D.he} left the pharmacy after the purchase, and I did not watch.\""), .cross("Does the receipt cover the other three robberies?", "\"No. It only covers the first one. I know nothing about where {D.he} was on the other days.\""), .cross("Did the defendant wear an orange vest?", "\"No. I did not see an orange vest. I only remember {DF} in ordinary clothes, and I do not recall any hat.\""), .cross("Do you know the defendant outside the pharmacy?", "\"No. I only know {DF} as a customer. I could not tell you anything about {DF}'s life.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} robbed four credit unions by note.", "A bus rider, a common slip, and a mistaken match."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry for what I did at the last branch.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} wrote notes in a notebook with the same threat wording.", "The notebook belonged to a man {DL} met at the shelter who took the bus daily."),
        defendant: [.direct("Tell the jury what you did on {DATE}.", "\"I robbed the last branch. I wrote the note and took the cash. I am ashamed of it, and I am not going to deny what I did.\""), .direct("Did you rob the other three credit unions?", "\"No. I did not. I only did the last one. I did not write any other notes, and I was not at those branches.\""), .direct("Why were you near the last branch?", "\"I needed money and I was desperate. I had been riding the bus every day, and the stop was right there.\""), .direct("What about the notebook with the same threat wording?", "\"I wrote notes in a notebook that belonged to a person I met at the shelter. That person rode the bus daily.\""), .direct("Where were you before the first robbery?", "\"Across town at a pharmacy. A receipt places me there about twenty minutes before the first robbery.\""), .direct("What was the orange vest?", "\"A work vest that I threw out. I used to wear it at a job, and I did not wear it for the first three robberies.\""), .cross("The fingerprint on the fourth slip is yours, isn't it?", "\"Yes. I wrote that one. I touched the slip, and I know the print is mine.\""), .cross("Your transit card was tapped at the stop after three robberies, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I ride that bus every day. That does not mean I robbed anyone. I am telling the truth about the last one.\""), .cross("You wrote notes in a notebook with the same threat wording, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I copied wording that the person from the shelter wrote. I did not know it was used in the other robberies.\""), .cross("Four branches were robbed the same way, weren't they?", "\"Yes. But I only did the last. The others were someone else, and I did not know who.\""), .cross("You threw the vest away, didn't you?", "\"Yes. After the last one. I was afraid it would connect me. I realize how that looks.\"")],
        openings: ("Over six weeks, four credit union branches were robbed the same way: a person in an orange vest and a ballcap wrote a threat on a deposit slip, took the cash, and walked to a bus stop. A fingerprint on the fourth slip matches {D}, and {D}'s transit card was tapped at the stop.", "The defense will present a pharmacy receipt that places {D} across town before the first robbery, a public counter where many hands touch slips, and a notebook that belonged to someone else. {D} admits only the last one."),
        closings: ("Four slips, four robberies, one print, and a transit card tapped at the stop after three of them. The same wording and the same vest tie the cases together, and the print is {D}'s.", "A bus rider who admits the last robbery, a pharmacy receipt for the first, a public counter, and a notebook that belonged to someone else. The State has not proved that {D} committed all four."),
        timeline: [(-42, "The first robbery."), (-28, "The second robbery."), (-14, "The third robbery."), (0, "The fourth robbery; the slip is saved.")],
        identified: "A fingerprint and a transit card.",
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof", "lesserIncluded"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let stalkerCoworkerV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.stalkerCoworker",
        category: .family,
        headlines: ["Woman Says Coworker Left Gifts and Followed Her to Church", "Doorbell Camera and Sticky Notes Back Stalking Charge"],
        law: "stalking",
        threshold: 6,
        spec: "Willfully harassed {V} on more than one occasion without legal purpose, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 24...55,
        victim: true,
        summary: "Over three months ending {DATE}, {V} found flowers and notes at {V.his} door, saw {D}, a coworker, in {V.his} church parking lot, and found {D}'s car parked down {V.his} street at night. {V} had told {D} twice to stop. A doorbell camera caught a person leaving a note. Sticky notes with {V}'s schedule were found in {D}'s work locker. {DL} says {D.he} lives nearby and attends the same church.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Doorbell Video", "A person in a work jacket leaves flowers and a note at {V}'s door at 6:10 a.m.; the face is partly hidden."), E(.document, 3, "Locker Notes", "Sticky notes with {V}'s shifts and gym times in {D}'s work locker.", .search), E(.document, 2, "Human Resources Complaint", "{V} told HR about the gifts and the parking lot.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 2, "Same Church", "{DL} has attended the same church for years."), E(.document, 2, "Lives Nearby", "{DL} lives two streets from {V}.")],
        role: "Victim",
        exam: [.direct("Tell us about your work and your coworkers.", "\"I work shifts at a business where {D} also works. We were coworkers, and I knew {DL} casually. I never thought of us as close.\""), .direct("What began to happen at your home?", "\"Over three months, I found flowers and notes at my door. At first I thought they were from a friend, but they did not stop.\""), .direct("What did the doorbell camera show?", "\"A person in a work jacket leaving flowers and a note at my door at 6:10 in the morning. The face is partly hidden.\""), .direct("What else did you notice?", "\"I saw {D.him} in my church parking lot. And {D.his} car was parked down my street at night, more than once.\""), .direct("Did you tell {D} to stop?", "\"Yes, twice. I told {DL} I did not want gifts or contact. {DL} did not stop, and I reported it to human resources.\""), .direct("What did the sticky notes in the locker say?", "\"They had my schedule written on them, including my shifts. They were found in {DL}'s work locker.\""), .cross("Did you see the defendant leave the notes at your door?", "\"Only on the video. The face is partly hidden, so I cannot say for certain that it was {DL}.\""), .cross("Does the defendant attend your church?", "\"Yes. {D.He} has attended the same church for years. That could explain why I saw {D.him} there, though not the other things.\""), .cross("Does the defendant live near you?", "\"Yes. {D.He} lives two streets from me. I did not know that until I looked into it.\""), .cross("Who else uses the locker?", "\"A coworker shares it with {D.him}. The notes in the locker could have come from that coworker.\""), .cross("Did the defendant keep a calendar of your shifts?", "\"I was told there was one on a phone note. I did not see it myself, and I do not know why it was there.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} followed and watched a coworker after being told to stop.", "A neighbor and fellow churchgoer."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry I frightened {V}.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} kept a calendar of {V}'s shifts on a phone note.", "The notes in the locker were from a coworker who shares the locker."),
        defendant: [.direct("Describe your relationship with {V} for the jury.", "\"We were coworkers. I thought we got along. I liked {V}, and I did not realize that {V} was uncomfortable with how I behaved.\""), .direct("Did you leave the notes and flowers?", "\"No. I did not. I do not know who left them. I did not go to {V}'s door that morning.\""), .direct("Why were you near {V}'s street?", "\"I live two streets away. I walk and drive through that area every day. I did not think anything of it.\""), .direct("Why do you go to the same church?", "\"I have attended it for years. I did not know {V} went there when I started, and I did not follow {V}.\""), .direct("What about the sticky notes in the locker?", "\"The locker is shared with another coworker. I did not write those notes, and I do not know whose they were.\""), .direct("Why did you keep a calendar of shifts?", "\"I keep track of the schedule for work. I wrote down several people's shifts, and {V}'s was one of them.\""), .cross("You were told twice to stop, weren't you?", "\"Yes. {V} told me twice. I did not think I was doing anything wrong, and I should have listened.\""), .cross("You saw {V} in the church parking lot, didn't you?", "\"Yes. It is a church I attend, so I see people there. I did not follow {V}.\""), .cross("Your car was parked down {V}'s street at night, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I live nearby, and I sometimes park there. I did not know it bothered anyone.\""), .cross("The sticky notes with {V}'s schedule were in your locker, weren't they?", "\"Yes. They were in the shared locker. I did not put them there, and I do not know who did.\""), .cross("You kept a calendar of {V}'s shifts on your phone, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I kept track of many people's shifts. I know how it looks, and I should not have recorded it.\"")],
        openings: ("Over three months, {V} found flowers and notes at the door, saw {D}, a coworker, in the church parking lot, and found {D}'s car parked down the street at night. {V} told {D} twice to stop, and a doorbell camera caught a person leaving a note.", "The defense will present a neighbor who lives two streets away, a fellow churchgoer, and a locker shared with another coworker. Living nearby and attending the same church is not stalking."),
        closings: ("Flowers, notes, a doorbell video, a locker full of schedules, a calendar of {V}'s shifts on {D}'s phone, and two requests to stop. {D} did not stop.", "A neighbor who attends the same church, and a locker shared with another coworker. The State has not proved that {D} left the notes or followed {V}."),
        timeline: [(-90, "The flowers begin."), (-45, "{D} seen in the church lot."), (-14, "{V} tells HR."), (0, "{V} reports to deputies.")],
        identified: "A doorbell camera and sticky notes.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        genders: ["V": .female])

